search-6","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#3-train-the-model-inside-your-harness-the-agent-plugin","content":"3\\. Train the model inside your harness (the agent plugin)"},"9":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-7","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#4-validation--test--scored-in-the-loop","content":"4\\. Validation & test — scored in the loop"},"10":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-8","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#5-metrics--measure-whatever-you-care-about","content":"5\\. Metrics — measure whatever you care about"},"11":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-9","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#6-logging--local-and-dashboard","content":"6\\. Logging — local and dashboard"},"12":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-10","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#7-write-the-conclusion-then-go-again","content":"7\\. Write the conclusion, then go again"},"13":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-11","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"8\\. Driving it with Claude Code"},"14":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-12","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch","content":"This page walks through the whole loop: **writing your own experiments with\nClaude Code** (or any coding agent). The agent reads what's been tried, launches\na new training run on Tinker, scores it, records what happened, and iterates —\ntoward a small model that beats frontier on your task at a fraction of the cost."},"15":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-13","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch","content":"Tinker-protocol infrastructure already made the hard part — GPUs, sharding, the\ntraining loop — someone else's problem. What's left is *research*: which **data**\nand which **recipe** win. That's the only thing the agent touches."},"16":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-14","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#1-every-experiment-is-standardised-and-stored","content":"For an agent to do research, it needs the **context of what's been tried**. So\nevery experiment carries two things:"},"17":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-15","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#1-every-experiment-is-standardised-and-stored","content":"a **hypothesis** — why you're running it, set in `metadata.hypothesis`;"},"18":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-16","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#1-every-experiment-is-standardised-and-stored","content":"a **conclusion** — what happened, auto-synthesized against your\n`success_metric` when the run finishes."},"19":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-17","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#1-every-experiment-is-standardised-and-stored","content":"Both are recorded and centralized. A Claude Code session therefore *starts* by\npulling the hypotheses and conclusions of past experiments — it instantly knows\nwhat's been tried and what worked, and proposes the next hypothesis. It doesn't\nre-derive anything; it just reads the record."},"20":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-18","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#2-launch-an-experiment","content":"The agent assembles one `ExperimentConfig`. It only ever controls the research —\nthe **data** and the **recipe** — and everything else is handled."},"21":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-19","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#custom-raw-data","content":"Point the config at a JSONL file; the agent curates what goes in (this is a\n**data ablation** — the first lever):"},"22":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-20","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#custom-transforms","content":"Raw rows become standardized **data-format rows** through an ordered list of\n`Transform`s. When the built-ins don't fit, the agent writes one — a class with\n`name` + `Config` and the `rows -> rows` contract, registered with a decorator:"},"23":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-21","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#custom-algorithm--any-algorithm-under-the-sun","content":"The recipe is one method. `BaseAlgorithm` owns all the plumbing (backend, step &\nsave cadence, evaluators, the training loop, checkpointing) and **is itself a\nStepBuilder*&#x2A; — a new algorithm only overrides &#x2A;*`build_batch()`** (and\noptionally `setup` / `step_metrics`). The loss rides on the returned\n`TrainingBatch`, so the agent writes only the heavy math — **any recipe, LoRA on\nany model**:"},"24":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-22","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#3-train-the-model-inside-your-harness-the-agent-plugin","content":"Here's the powerful part for agentic workloads: the **rollout harness is itself\npluggable**. By default RL rolls out with a simple chat agent, but you can\nregister &#x2A;*any harbor `BaseAgent`** — a multi-turn, tool-using harness — and\npoint the algorithm at it:"},"25":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-23","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#3-train-the-model-inside-your-harness-the-agent-plugin","content":"The model then trains **inside that harness** — taking turns, calling your\ntools, getting rewarded on the outcome — so it **learns to use the harness\nitself**. This is exactly how Opus is trained inside the Claude Code harness:\nregister your harness, and the model you train learns to operate in it. The\nagent harness is the third lever."},"26":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-24","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#4-validation--test--scored-in-the-loop","content":"Every run is tied to real task performance by scoring it against benchmarks\nunder `metadata.benchmark`. Two **independent** knobs:"},"27":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-25","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#4-validation--test--scored-in-the-loop","content":"**`run_every`** decides *when* an entry is scored: `run_every: N` scores it\n**in-loop every N steps**; omit `run_every` and it's scored **once, after\ntraining**. This applies to any entry."},"28":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-26","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#4-validation--test--scored-in-the-loop","content":"**`split`** (`val` / `test`) is just a **label** that namespaces the metrics so\ndifferent benchmarks' scores stay apart in the logs — it does *not* decide\nwhen an entry runs. A `test` benchmark can run in-loop too; just give it a\n`run_every`."},"29":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-27","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#4-validation--test--scored-in-the-loop","content":"In-loop evals run as **async rollouts** on Harbor's engine, so evaluation\noverlaps training rather than stalling it."},"30":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-28","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#5-metrics--measure-whatever-you-care-about","content":"A benchmark's `metrics` come from the **metric registry**: score rollouts however\n*you* define success — `pass@1`, `pass@3`, `pass^3`, or the economics that come\nfree from Harbor usage (**cost / time / tokens** per task)."},"31":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-29","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#5-metrics--measure-whatever-you-care-about","content":"The contract is one method — a metric receives the **per-task rewards** (one\ninner list per task, one reward per sampled rollout) and returns a single\nnumber. There's no `Config`; a metric takes no params:"},"32":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-30","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#6-logging--local-and-dashboard","content":"The agent *reads* its experiments through logging. Add either or both via\n`callbacks`:"},"33":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-31","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#6-logging--local-and-dashboard","content":"**`local_logger`** writes per-step `metrics.jsonl` (train + val rows, split\ntagged), `predictions/`, a per-run `summary.md`, **and*&#x2A; an experiment-level\n**`experiment.md` containing the hypothesis and the final conclusion** — so the\nwhole research record lives on disk, no dashboard required."},"34":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-32","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#6-logging--local-and-dashboard","content":"**`evsys_logger`** pushes the same record (metrics, predictions, hypothesis,\nconclusion) to the EvolvingSystems dashboard via `EVSYS_API_KEY` for a\ncentralized, cross-experiment history."},"35":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-33","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#7-write-the-conclusion-then-go-again","content":"When the run finishes, the SDK scores the arms against your `success_metric&#x60;,\npicks the &#x2A;*`best_arm`**, and synthesizes a **conclusion** — recorded right next\nto the hypothesis (in `experiment.md` and/or the dashboard). Claude Code reads\nthat conclusion, updates its hypothesis, and launches the next experiment."},"36":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-34","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#7-write-the-conclusion-then-go-again","content":"That's the autoresearch loop:"},"37":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-35","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#7-write-the-conclusion-then-go-again","content":"> **read past hypotheses + conclusions → form a hypothesis → launch → score →\n> write a conclusion → repeat.**"},"38":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-36","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#7-write-the-conclusion-then-go-again","content":"A sweep makes each step wider: declare a `matrix` and one YAML expands into many\narms (run concurrently), so the agent searches learning rates and methods in\nparallel and keeps the best:"},"39":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-37","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"Load `evsys-sdk` as a **Claude Code plugin** and the agent gets skills + a\ntraining agent that already know this whole flow, so it launches *better*\nexperiments instead of starting cold:"},"40":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-38","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"**`set-up-research-project`** — scaffold a repo into the standard\n`data/ · src/ · experiments/ · .evsys/` layout."},"41":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-39","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"**`using-the-sdk`** — author correct configs, transforms, and algorithms."},"42":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-40","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"the &#x2A;*`training-decider`** agent — read prior context and materialize the next\nexperiment end-to-end."},"43":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-41","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"Every registry you can plug into."},"44":{"id":"/docs/autoresearch-42","page_id":"/docs/autoresearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/autoresearch#8-driving-it-with-claude-code","content":"SFT · RL · SDFT, step by step."},"45":{"id":"/docs/cookbook","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"page","content":"Cookbook","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook"},"46":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-0","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook","content":"End-to-end walkthroughs for the most common tasks."},"47":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-1","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#cookbook","content":"Cookbook"},"48":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-2","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#setup","content":"Setup"},"49":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-3","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#1-hello-world-no-gpu-no-network","content":"1\\. Hello world (no GPU, no network)"},"50":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-4","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#2-drive-everything-from-yaml","content":"2\\. Drive everything from YAML"},"51":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-5","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#3-matrix-campaigns","content":"3\\. Matrix campaigns"},"52":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-6","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#4-adding-your-own-algorithm","content":"4\\. Adding your own algorithm"},"53":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-7","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#5-adding-your-own-verifier-reward-function","content":"5\\. Adding your own verifier (reward function)"},"54":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-8","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#6-real-tinker-sft","content":"6\\. Real Tinker SFT"},"55":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-9","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#cli","content":"CLI"},"56":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-10","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#architecture-map","content":"Architecture map"},"57":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-11","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"Stores: local vs Supabase"},"58":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-12","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#backends","content":"Backends"},"59":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-13","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Modular extension cheat sheet"},"60":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-14","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#cookbook","content":"Walkthroughs for the most common things you'll do with `evsys-sdk`."},"61":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-15","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#setup","content":"For real Tinker training, also `export TINKER_API_KEY=...`."},"62":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-16","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#setup","content":"Run unit tests:"},"63":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-17","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#1-hello-world-no-gpu-no-network","content":"`examples/01_local_mock_sft.py` runs a deterministic mock SFT. It's the\nfastest way to verify the framework is wired up right."},"64":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-18","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#1-hello-world-no-gpu-no-network","content":"You should see a `final_checkpoint` artifact and a `metrics.jsonl` in\n`examples/outputs/01/.../logs/`."},"65":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-19","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#2-drive-everything-from-yaml","content":"`examples/02_yaml_driven.py` shows the same experiment expressed as a YAML\nstring. The library's canonical interface is YAML — Python configs are just\nsugar that produces the same dict tree. This is what an external evolution\nloop should mutate."},"66":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-20","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#3-matrix-campaigns","content":"`examples/03_matrix_campaign.py` shows a 6-run sweep from one `matrix:` block.\nFor real campaigns (e.g. LoRA-rank × SFT-checkpoint fan-out), this is what\nyou'd write for a LoRA-rank × checkpoint fan-out."},"67":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-21","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#4-adding-your-own-algorithm","content":"`examples/04_custom_algorithm.py` registers a new training recipe via\n`@register_algorithm(\"cosine_toy\")`. The decorator + Pydantic Config is the\nentire integration; YAMLs can immediately use `kind: cosine_toy`."},"68":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-22","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#4-adding-your-own-algorithm","content":"For external packages that should auto-extend the registry, declare an entry\npoint in your `pyproject.toml`:"},"69":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-23","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#4-adding-your-own-algorithm","content":"When `evsys_sdk` imports, every entry point in that group is\nloaded. No fork needed."},"70":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-24","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#5-adding-your-own-verifier-reward-function","content":"`examples/05_custom_verifier.py` registers a Gaussian length-reward verifier.\nSame pattern as algorithms; entry point group is\n`evsys_sdk.verifiers`."},"71":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-25","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#6-real-tinker-sft","content":"`examples/06_tinker_sft_real.py` — minimal real Tinker run, costs roughly $0.01."},"72":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-26","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#6-real-tinker-sft","content":"For a real-world campaign you'd write a SFT-then-RL fan-out over LoRA rank with\ncheckpointing at 50/75/90/100% of training steps, then evaluate everything and\nproduce a single combined plot."},"73":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-27","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#architecture-map","content":"Every box on the right is one extension point with its own registry and\nentry-point group."},"74":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-28","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"The library defines `DataStore` and `LogStore` as protocols (see\n`src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py`). Built-in implementations:"},"75":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-29","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"`LocalDataStore` (root-anchored filesystem JSONL/JSON)"},"76":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-30","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"`InMemoryDataStore` (test-only)"},"77":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-31","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"`JSONLLogStore` (append-only metrics.jsonl + hyperparams.json + artifacts.json)"},"78":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-32","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"`TensorBoardLogStore` (SummaryWriter)"},"79":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-33","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"`MultiplexLogStore` (fan-out to N children)"},"80":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-34","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#stores-local-vs-supabase","content":"Supabase adapters live in `evsys_sdk.adapters.supabase` (extra:\n`pip install evsys-sdk[supabase]`). They are optional — the core\nlibrary imports zero Supabase code."},"81":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-35","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#backends","content":"Pick `mock` for tests, `local` for local TRL training, `tinker` for hosted\nTinker training. Algorithms are routed to the right code path based on\n`ctx.backend.name`."},"82":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-36","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Extension point"},"83":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-37","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Decorator"},"84":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-38","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Entry point group"},"85":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-39","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Algorithm"},"86":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-40","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_algorithm(\"name\")`"},"87":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-41","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.algorithms`"},"88":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-42","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Verifier"},"89":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-43","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_verifier(\"name\")`"},"90":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-44","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.verifiers`"},"91":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-45","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Metric"},"92":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-46","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_metric(\"name\")`"},"93":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-47","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.metrics`"},"94":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-48","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Backend"},"95":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-49","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_backend(\"name\")`"},"96":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-50","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.backends`"},"97":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-51","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"InferenceClient"},"98":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-52","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_inference(\"name\")`"},"99":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-53","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.inference`"},"100":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-54","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Transform"},"101":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-55","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_transform(\"name\")`"},"102":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-56","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.transforms`"},"103":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-57","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"DataStore"},"104":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-58","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_data_store(\"name\")`"},"105":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-59","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.data_stores`"},"106":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-60","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"LogStore"},"107":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-61","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`@register_log_store(\"name\")`"},"108":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-62","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"`evsys_sdk.log_stores`"},"109":{"id":"/docs/cookbook-63","page_id":"/docs/cookbook","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cookbook#modular-extension-cheat-sheet","content":"Each registered class declares a `Config: ClassVar[type]` Pydantic model that\ndefines the legal field space — this is exactly what an evolutionary\nalgorithm needs to know to mutate the YAML safely."},"110":{"id":"/docs/design","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"page","content":"Design & Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design"},"111":{"id":"/docs/design-0","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design","content":"Layout, protocols, and the rationale behind the SDK."},"112":{"id":"/docs/design-1","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#evsys-sdk--design-notes","content":"evsys-sdk — design notes"},"113":{"id":"/docs/design-2","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#goals","content":"Goals"},"114":{"id":"/docs/design-3","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#why-protocols-not-abcs","content":"Why protocols, not ABCs"},"115":{"id":"/docs/design-4","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#why-a-registry-per-kind","content":"Why a registry per kind"},"116":{"id":"/docs/design-5","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#yaml-schema","content":"YAML schema"},"117":{"id":"/docs/design-6","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Lifecycle of a run"},"118":{"id":"/docs/design-7","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#researcher-project-layout","content":"Researcher-project layout"},"119":{"id":"/docs/design-8","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#referencing-data-by-id--name-preferred-over-local-paths","content":"Referencing data by id / name (preferred over local paths)"},"120":{"id":"/docs/design-9","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#benchmark-test-vs-validation-in-loop","content":"Benchmark (test) vs. validation (in-loop)"},"121":{"id":"/docs/design-10","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"OOP entry points"},"122":{"id":"/docs/design-11","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"What's NOT in v0.1"},"123":{"id":"/docs/design-12","page_id":"/docs/design","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design#backwards-compatibility","content":"Backwards compatibility"},"124":{"id":"/docs/design-13","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#goals","content":"**Single declarative YAML** drives a full experiment (data → train → eval),\nso an evolutionary algorithm can mutate it without writing Python."},"125":{"id":"/docs/design-14","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#goals","content":"**Modular** — adding a new algorithm/verifier/metric is a decorator + a\nPydantic Config class. No library fork."},"126":{"id":"/docs/design-15","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#goals","content":"**Backend-pluggable** — same YAML can run locally on TRL or remotely on\nTinker; backends are interchangeable."},"127":{"id":"/docs/design-16","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#goals","content":"**Decoupled storage** — the library imports zero Supabase code by default;\nSupabase is an optional adapter."},"128":{"id":"/docs/design-17","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#why-protocols-not-abcs","content":"PEP 544 protocols mean any class with the right methods satisfies the contract\n— no inheritance from us. This is critical for third-party extensions: if you\nhave to subclass `evsys_sdk.algorithms.BaseAlgorithm`, you've\nimported the world. With protocols, your `MyDPO` class is just plain Python."},"129":{"id":"/docs/design-18","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#why-a-registry-per-kind","content":"Each extension point has its own registry (`_algorithms`, `_verifiers`, …).\nReasons:"},"130":{"id":"/docs/design-19","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#why-a-registry-per-kind","content":"The YAML loader knows which registry to look up `kind:` in based on the\nsurrounding context. No string-prefix tricks."},"131":{"id":"/docs/design-20","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#why-a-registry-per-kind","content":"`schema_for(kind, name)` exposes the per-extension JSON schema, which is\nexactly what an evolution algorithm needs to mutate the YAML safely."},"132":{"id":"/docs/design-21","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#why-a-registry-per-kind","content":"Per-extension entry-point groups mean external packages declare their\ncontributions cleanly."},"133":{"id":"/docs/design-22","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#yaml-schema","content":"Strict Pydantic v2: every field has a type, `extra='forbid'` everywhere, no\ndefaults that hide misspellings. The `kind:` discriminator selects which\nregistered class's `Config` validates the corresponding `params:` block."},"134":{"id":"/docs/design-23","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#yaml-schema","content":"The `matrix:` shorthand is a convenience that expands at load-time into\n`runs:` — the result is the same `runs[]` shape, so the runner doesn't care."},"135":{"id":"/docs/design-24","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"`run_experiment(cfg)` → for each `RunConfig`:"},"136":{"id":"/docs/design-25","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Build `data_store`, `log_store` from top-level specs."},"137":{"id":"/docs/design-26","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Read raw rows via `data_store`."},"138":{"id":"/docs/design-27","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Apply `data.transforms[]` in order."},"139":{"id":"/docs/design-28","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Build `backend`, call `backend.prepare(model=..., run_dir=...)` → handles dict."},"140":{"id":"/docs/design-29","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Build `algorithm` with `params`."},"141":{"id":"/docs/design-30","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Construct `RunContext` carrying `data_store`, `log_store`, `backend`, `extras`."},"142":{"id":"/docs/design-31","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"`algorithm.train(ctx)` → `RunResult`."},"143":{"id":"/docs/design-32","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"`backend.teardown(handles)`."},"144":{"id":"/docs/design-33","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Best-effort eval (skips on failure — eval errors don't fail the run)."},"145":{"id":"/docs/design-34","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#lifecycle-of-a-run","content":"Persist `run_result.json`."},"146":{"id":"/docs/design-35","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#researcher-project-layout","content":"Every project the training-decider agent bootstraps follows the same shape so\nscripts, benchmarks, and extensions land in predictable places. Scaffold a new\nproject with `evsys init-project <name>`; the tree is:"},"147":{"id":"/docs/design-36","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#researcher-project-layout","content":"Each `config.yaml` is **self-contained** — there is no project-root yaml that\nexperiments inherit from. The experiment-level fields (hypothesis, tags,\nsuccess\\_metric, benchmark) live under `metadata:` and are read by\n`Experiment.run()`:"},"148":{"id":"/docs/design-37","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#referencing-data-by-id--name-preferred-over-local-paths","content":"Stored experiment scripts should reference data by **dashboard id** (or\n**name**, which resolves to the latest version's id) rather than a local path.\nThe SDK pulls the rows once into the local `.evsys/` workspace cache and\ntrains/scores from there, so a committed script is portable and doesn't depend\non anyone's local file layout. `path` stays as an offline / dev fallback."},"149":{"id":"/docs/design-38","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#referencing-data-by-id--name-preferred-over-local-paths","content":"Same for the benchmark block above (`id` / `name` / `path`). Under the hood\nboth go through `Workspace.pull_dataset` / `pull_benchmark`, which cache to\n`.evsys/<datasets|benchmarks>/<id>.jsonl` (version-immutable, so a given\nid never changes)."},"150":{"id":"/docs/design-39","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#benchmark-test-vs-validation-in-loop","content":"Both test and validation are entries in the same `metadata.benchmark` list;\n`tags` declare the role and `run_every` declares the cadence."},"151":{"id":"/docs/design-40","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#benchmark-test-vs-validation-in-loop","content":"A **test benchmark** is the *final goal*: scored once after training (no\n`run_every`), tagged `[test]`. Model selection must never key off it."},"152":{"id":"/docs/design-41","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#benchmark-test-vs-validation-in-loop","content":"A **validation benchmark** is scored *during* training to drive model\nselection — same harbor format, tagged `[val]` with a positive\n`run_every`:"},"153":{"id":"/docs/design-42","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#benchmark-test-vs-validation-in-loop","content":"Every `run_every` steps the training loop scores the live model on the\n`[val]` entry and records `val/<name>/<metric>` curves under\n`split=\"val\"` — separate from the post-training `[test]` eval."},"154":{"id":"/docs/design-43","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"The high-level path is one class with declarative inputs:"},"155":{"id":"/docs/design-44","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"`Experiment` owns:"},"156":{"id":"/docs/design-45","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"creating the dashboard experiment + per-arm run records;"},"157":{"id":"/docs/design-46","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"expanding `matrix` / `Sweep` into one `RunConfig` per arm;"},"158":{"id":"/docs/design-47","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"per-arm failure isolation (one arm raising doesn't kill the sweep);"},"159":{"id":"/docs/design-48","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"post-train benchmark scoring via `Benchmark.score(client)`;"},"160":{"id":"/docs/design-49","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"auto-forwarding the local `metrics.jsonl` to the store\n(no manual `backfill_step_metrics` call);"},"161":{"id":"/docs/design-50","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"aggregating `best_score` + `conclusion` and finalizing the experiment."},"162":{"id":"/docs/design-51","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#oop-entry-points","content":"The legacy `run_experiment(cfg)` is still the inner runner that\n`Experiment` calls per arm — bypass `Experiment` only when you need to do\ntraining without dashboard bookkeeping."},"163":{"id":"/docs/design-52","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"Supabase adapters (planned: `evsys_sdk.adapters.supabase`)."},"164":{"id":"/docs/design-53","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"Evolutionary loop (kept in `backend/api/experiments/loop.py` for now)."},"165":{"id":"/docs/design-54","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"Distributed launchers (Modal, Slurm)."},"166":{"id":"/docs/design-55","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"Streaming / checkpoint resumption beyond what tinker\\_cookbook provides."},"167":{"id":"/docs/design-56","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#whats-not-in-v01","content":"These all extend the same protocol surface and should arrive incrementally\nwithout breaking changes to the public API."},"168":{"id":"/docs/design-57","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#backwards-compatibility","content":"`version: 1` in the YAML root is currently advisory; bumped on schema breaks."},"169":{"id":"/docs/design-58","page_id":"/docs/design","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design#backwards-compatibility","content":"Public symbols re-exported from `evsys_sdk/__init__.py` are the\nstable surface. Anything else may move."},"170":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"171":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"A declarative framework for LLM training experiments — SFT, RL, and distillation from a single YAML, built so coding agents can launch experiments, learn from them, and train models continuously."},"172":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#-coding-agents-customise","content":"🧑‍💻 Coding agents customise"},"173":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"⚙️ The SDK handles everything else"},"174":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"What you can plug in"},"175":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"176":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"We believe there will not be a few generally intelligent models that everyone\nuses, but **thousands of models adapted for every task**, continually learning\nfrom every interaction. To enable this we need infrastructure that lets\n**coding agents launch experiments, learn from them, and train models that\nlearn continuously**. `evsys-sdk` is the first step toward that."},"177":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"This is the whole point of `evsys-sdk`: &#x2A;*turn your favourite coding agent into\na model lab.**"},"178":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"To enable autoresearch we need **standardisation** of experiments — and\n`evsys-sdk` standardises every experiment while staying flexible enough to run\n**any algorithm on any data**."},"179":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Tinker-protocol training infrastructure has made the hard part — provisioning\nGPUs, sharding, the training loop — someone else's problem. What's left is the\n*research*: which **data** and which **recipe** produce a model that wins on\nyour task. `evsys-sdk` makes that research the only thing you (and your agent)\ntouch, and standardizes + centralizes every experiment so the agent always has\nthe context of what's been tried."},"180":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"So the loop becomes: your coding agent — **Claude Code**, **Codex**, anything —\nwrites a config, launches it on the tinker backend, reads the structured\nresult, and writes the next one. Run a series of educated experiments and you\nland a small, task-specific model that **beats frontier on your task at a\nfraction of the cost** — driven entirely by the agent."},"181":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"An experiment is a single YAML file."},"182":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#-coding-agents-customise","content":"**Data ablations** — what data goes into training (sources, mixes, transforms)."},"183":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#-coding-agents-customise","content":"**Algorithmic changes** — only the heavy math: override `build_batch()` and the loss."},"184":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Experiment orchestration** — sweeps, arms, seeds, failure isolation, conclusions."},"185":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Data** — loading, caching & lineage → data format rows."},"186":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**The training loop** — forward/backward, optimizer steps, save cadence."},"187":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Checkpointing & artifacts.**"},"188":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Evaluation** — in-loop validation + benchmark scoring, metrics & verifiers."},"189":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Backends & compute** — mock / local / tinker, rollouts via Harbor."},"190":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#️-the-sdk-handles-everything-else","content":"**Logging, dashboard & storage.**"},"191":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"Every moving part is a registry: reference a built-in by name in the YAML, or\nregister your own with a one-line `@register_*` decorator — no fork."},"192":{"id":"/docs-21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Tinker-compatible backends** — train on anything that exposes the Tinker\ntraining server: Fireworks, TML, SkyRL, … one line in the config switches provider."},"193":{"id":"/docs-22","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Algorithms** — any recipe under the sun (SFT, RL, distillation, or your\nown), LoRA on any model — defined by overriding a single `build_batch()`."},"194":{"id":"/docs-23","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Agent harnesses** — train a model *inside* your own multi-turn harness (any\nharbor `BaseAgent`) so it learns to use your tools — the way Opus is trained\ninside the Claude Code harness."},"195":{"id":"/docs-24","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Transforms** — turn any raw data into the standard data-format rows; chain\nbuilt-ins or register your own."},"196":{"id":"/docs-25","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Verifiers** — the reward / correctness check for RL and eval\n(`exact_match`, `contains`, LLM-judge, or custom)."},"197":{"id":"/docs-26","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Metrics** — score rollouts however you measure success: `pass@1`, `pass@3`,\ncost, latency, your own."},"198":{"id":"/docs-27","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Validation & evaluation** — score against benchmarks via `metadata.benchmark`:\n`run_every: N` scores in-loop every N steps (omit it to score once after\ntraining); the `split` tag (`val`/`test`) just separates the metrics."},"199":{"id":"/docs-28","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Inference clients** — how eval / RL query a model to generate."},"200":{"id":"/docs-29","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Data & log stores** — where data is read and where metrics/artifacts are\nwritten (local files, the dashboard, TensorBoard)."},"201":{"id":"/docs-30","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Callbacks** — hook the training lifecycle for logging, early stopping, or\ndashboard upload."},"202":{"id":"/docs-31","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-you-can-plug-in","content":"**Deployers** — ship the trained adapter (e.g. F