tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#5-matrix-campaigns","content":"**Axis keys are dotted paths** into the run dict (`_set_dotted`)."},"479":{"id":"/docs/reference-239","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#5-matrix-campaigns","content":"**`name_template`** uses literal `{dotted.key}` placeholders (not\n`str.format`, so dots aren't attribute access) plus `{base}` = base run name.\nFloats are slugged (`1e-4` → `0p0001`-style via `%g`, `+`/`.` stripped)."},"480":{"id":"/docs/reference-240","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#5-matrix-campaigns","content":"Without a template, names become `{base}__{lastkey}{value}__...`."},"481":{"id":"/docs/reference-241","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#5-matrix-campaigns","content":"The 3×2 example above yields **6 runs**."},"482":{"id":"/docs/reference-242","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"`run_experiment(cfg_or_path)` (in `runner.py`) accepts an `ExperimentConfig` or\na YAML path, expands matrix, then for **each** `RunConfig` calls `_execute_run`:"},"483":{"id":"/docs/reference-243","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Build stores** from the top-level specs. For `jsonl`/`tensorboard` log\nstores (and `multiplex` children), `log_dir` is auto-filled to\n`<run_dir>/logs[/kind]` if not set."},"484":{"id":"/docs/reference-244","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Build backend** from `run.backend`."},"485":{"id":"/docs/reference-245","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Load rows** via `_load_rows` (dispatch on `source_kind`)."},"486":{"id":"/docs/reference-246","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Apply transforms** in order (`_apply_transforms`); each transform is called\nas `transform(rows) -> rows`."},"487":{"id":"/docs/reference-247","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Build algorithm** from the registry with `run.algorithm.params`."},"488":{"id":"/docs/reference-248","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**`backend.prepare(model=..., run_dir=...)`** → a dict of handles. &#x2A;If this\nraises, the run is recorded `status=\"failed\"` and returned early.*"},"489":{"id":"/docs/reference-249","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Construct `RunContext`** carrying stores, backend, and an `extras` dict\n(`train_rows`, `n_train_rows`, `backend_handles`, `model_name`, `tags`)."},"490":{"id":"/docs/reference-250","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**`log_store.log_hyperparams(...)`** (experiment/run name, model, backend, tags)."},"491":{"id":"/docs/reference-251","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**`algorithm.train(ctx) -> RunResult`** inside try/finally; on exception →\n`status=\"failed\"`. `backend.teardown(handles)` always runs in `finally`."},"492":{"id":"/docs/reference-252","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**Eval (best-effort)** — only if `status == \"completed\"`. Any eval exception\nis logged and swallowed; **eval never fails the run**. Eval metrics are\nmerged into `result.metrics` under `eval/<metric_kind>` keys and logged."},"493":{"id":"/docs/reference-253","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"**`log_store.close()`** then **persist** `run_dir/run_result.json`\n(`run_id`, `status`, `metrics`, `artifacts`, `error`, `hparams`, `ts`)."},"494":{"id":"/docs/reference-254","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"The eval loop (`_run_eval`) builds the inference client from\n`eval.inference`, generates for each row (prompt = `row[\"prompt\"]` or the last\nmessage content), extracts `<answer>…</answer>` if present, and compares against\ntargets (`tool_slug`/`answer` + `toolkit`) using each configured `Metric`."},"495":{"id":"/docs/reference-255","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#6-the-run-lifecycle","content":"> Note: validation of `params` against each `.Config` is **lazy** by default\n> (happens at instantiation in the runner). `evsys validate --deep` /\n> `validate_yaml(path, deep=True)` forces it up front so unknown entry-point\n> extensions don't fail prematurely."},"496":{"id":"/docs/reference-256","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#7-extension-points--protocols","content":"Defined in `protocols.py`. Most are `@runtime_checkable` so the registry can\ngive better errors. Every extension declares `name: ClassVar[str]` (registry\nkey); most also declare `Config: ClassVar[type]` (a Pydantic model for `params`)."},"497":{"id":"/docs/reference-257","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#run-dataclasses-passed-to-every-algorithm","content":"**`RunContext`** — everything an algorithm needs:\n`run_id`, `output_dir`, `config` (the parsed `ExperimentConfig`), `data_store`,\n`log_store`, `backend`, `extras: dict` (free bag — e.g. `train_rows`,\n`backend_handles`, tinker `training_client`)."},"498":{"id":"/docs/reference-258","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#run-dataclasses-passed-to-every-algorithm","content":"**`RunResult`** — what `train` returns:\n`run_id`, `status` 