OJECT_ID`"},"605":{"id":"/docs/reference-365","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"—"},"606":{"id":"/docs/reference-366","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"Shared per-project id"},"607":{"id":"/docs/reference-367","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"`EVSYS_LOG_DIR`"},"608":{"id":"/docs/reference-368","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"`./evsys_sdk`"},"609":{"id":"/docs/reference-369","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"Local mirror dir"},"610":{"id":"/docs/reference-370","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"`EVSYS_OFFLINE`"},"611":{"id":"/docs/reference-371","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"`false`"},"612":{"id":"/docs/reference-372","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"Local-mirror-only, no auth"},"613":{"id":"/docs/reference-373","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"`EVSYS_LOGGING_LEVEL`"},"614":{"id":"/docs/reference-374","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"—"},"615":{"id":"/docs/reference-375","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"SDK log level"},"616":{"id":"/docs/reference-376","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"**`ExperimentRun`** is a context-manager wrapper for the common flow:"},"617":{"id":"/docs/reference-377","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#13-dashboard-client","content":"Lower-level client methods: `create_experiment`, `update_experiment`,\n`create_generation`, `update_generation`, `log_step_metric`, `log_eval_run`,\n`log_predictions`, `record_benchmark`. `ExperimentRun` also exposes\n`log_predictions`, `update_generation/experiment`, and a `benchmark(...)`\ncontext. SDK write routes live under `API_PREFIX = /api/dashboard/api`\n(e.g. `/sdk/experiments/`, `/sdk/generations/{id}/step/`)."},"618":{"id":"/docs/reference-378","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"Everything importable from `evsys_sdk` (the stable surface;\nanything not re-exported here may move):"},"619":{"id":"/docs/reference-379","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Config models:** `ExperimentConfig`, `RunConfig`, `AlgorithmConfig`,\n`DataConfig`, `ModelConfig`, `BackendConfig`, `EvalConfig`, `DataStoreSpec`,\n`LogStoreSpec`, `MetricSpec`, `VerifierSpec`, `TransformSpec`, `InferenceSpec`."},"620":{"id":"/docs/reference-380","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Protocols & run types:** `Algorithm`, `Backend`, `DataStore`, `LogStore`,\n`Metric`, `Verifier`, `Transform`, `InferenceClient`, `RunContext`, `RunResult`."},"621":{"id":"/docs/reference-381","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**YAML:** `load_yaml`, `dump_yaml`, `validate_yaml`."},"622":{"id":"/docs/reference-382","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Registry:** `register_*` / `get_*` / `list_*` for all 8 kinds."},"623":{"id":"/docs/reference-383","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Runner:** `run_experiment`."},"624":{"id":"/docs/reference-384","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Data shapes:** `TargetFormat`, `ChatMessagesRow`, `HarborTask`,\n`PromptExample`, the three verifier specs + `VerifierPayload`, block helpers,\n`detect_format`, `from_dict`, `to_dict`, `iter_jsonl`."},"625":{"id":"/docs/reference-385","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Dashboard:** `DashboardClient`, `ExperimentRun`, `DashboardClientError`,\n`EvsysAuthError`."},"626":{"id":"/docs/reference-386","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#14-public-api-surface","content":"**Logging:** `configure_logger`, `get_logger`, `set_level`."},"627":{"id":"/docs/reference-387","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#15-relationship-to-the-backend-repo","content":"The SDK is the **external, declarative front end** to the production training\nstack in `backend/api/experiments/`:"},"628":{"id":"/docs/reference-388","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#15-relationship-to-the-backend-repo","content":"`backend/api/experiments/types.py` is the **source of truth**: a richly typed\ntree of frozen dataclasses (`Experiment`, `GenerationConfig`, `DataPipeline`,\nconcrete `SFT/RL/SDFT/Combo/PromptTuning` recipes, `Tinker/MLX/Modal` backends,\n`EvalPlan`, …) with compatibility validation baked into `__post_init__`."},"629":{"id":"/docs/reference-389","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#15-relationship-to-the-backend-repo","content":"The SDK **flattens** that into generic `kind`+`params` Pydantic envelopes\nresolved against registries at load time, so an evolution loop can mutate YAML\nwithout importing the typed classes."},"630":{"id":"/docs/reference-390","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#15-relationship-to-the-backend-repo","content":"The SDK's `data_types.py` mirrors **only** the row/verifier shapes\n(`ChatMessagesRow`, `HarborTask`, `PromptExample`, the three verifiers) so\nJSONL round-trips between the two stacks without conversion."},"631":{"id":"/docs/reference-391","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#15-relationship-to-the-backend-repo","content":"The SDK's run-result types (`RunContext`, `RunResult`, `VerificationResult`)\nlive in `protocols.py` rather than as an `Experiment` campaign object."},"632":{"id":"/docs/reference-392","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#not-in-v01-per-docsdesignmd","content":"Supabase data/log adapters (`evsys_sdk.adapters.supabase`), the\nevolutionary loop port, distributed launchers (Modal/Slurm), and checkpoint\nresumption beyond what `tinker_cookbook` provides. All extend the same protocol\nsurface and are expected to arrive without breaking the public API."},"633":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","type":"page","content":"Algorithms & Evaluation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms"},"634":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","content":"One contract — train(ctx) -> RunResult — plus an optional gradient toolkit and a test/validation firewall."},"635":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#algorithm","content":"Algorithm"},"636":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#evaluation--a-testvalidation-firewall","content":"Evaluation — a test/validation firewall"},"637":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"Metrics & Verifiers"},"638":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","content":"The algorithm surface is **one required contract** (`train(ctx) -> RunResult`)\nplus an optional gradient toolkit and pluggable evaluation. It runs over any\ntinker-compatible `Backend` — `mock` for tests, `local` for TRL+peft, `tinker`\nfor hosted."},"639":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#algorithm","content":"`Algorithm` (protocol): `name`, `Config`, `train(ctx) -> RunResult`. The only\nrequired contract — `train()` may do anything. The optional toolkit:\n`TrainingLoop` drives the gradient loop; a `StepBuilder` (`build_batch ->\nTrainingBatch`) is the unit of \"a new gradient method\"; losses are a **named\nstring*&#x2A; or a &#x2A;*`LossCallable`** (client-side, via `forward_backward_custom`)."},"640":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#evaluation--a-testvalidation-firewall","content":"**Benchmark** — the *test set*, scored **once after** training. Model\nselection must never key off it."},"641":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#evaluation--a-testvalidation-firewall","content":"**Validation** — scored **in-loop** every N steps to drive selection."},"642":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#evaluation--a-testvalidation-firewall","content":"Both are harbor-format and scored via the **Metric** / **Verifier** registries."},"643":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"**`Metric`**: `compute(predictions, targets) -> float`."},"644":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"**`Verifier`**: `verify(prompt, completion, target) -> reward` (RL reward or\nper-task scoring)."},"645":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"**`InferenceClient`**: `generate(...)` — how eval/RL query a model."},"646":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"A `Benchmark` is your held-out test. If you select the best arm using\nbenchmark scores, you've leaked the test set — use `Validation` for selection."},"647":{"id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/algorithms#metrics--verifiers","content":"Next: Extensibility ·\nalgorithms API."},"648":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/architecture"},"649":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture","content":"The whole system at a glance — one ExperimentConfig, five layers, eight registries."},"650":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"The Experiment — the organizing unit"},"651":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"The five layers"},"652":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture","content":"`evsys-sdk` is organized around a single idea: **one `ExperimentConfig` (YAML)\ndrives everything**, and every `kind:` in it resolves through a registry."},"653":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"The **Experiment** is the top of the system. It's the scientific container: you\ngive it a hypothesis and one or more runs, and it produces a best arm and an\nauto-synthesized conclusion. Concretely, `Experiment.run()`:"},"654":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"**Expands** the config — a single `run`, a list of `runs`, or a `matrix`\nshorthand — into one or more **arms** (each arm is one `RunConfig` = one\ntraining job). `n_repeats` replicates an arm across seeds for variance."},"655":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"**Runs each arm** through the same pipeline — **Data → Training →\nEvaluation** — with per-arm failure isolation."},"656":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"**Picks the best arm** by your `success_metric` and records an\n`ExperimentResult` (`best_arm`, `conclusion`, metrics)."},"657":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-experiment--the-organizing-unit","content":"So an experiment is *one YAML* that can fan out into a whole campaign of runs,\neach of which is the left-to-right pipeline you saw on the\nintroduction. Blue is what you author; white pillars and the grey\nresult are what the SDK owns."},"658":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Layer"},"659":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"What it does"},"660":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Start here"},"661":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"**① Experiment**"},"662":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"The organizing unit — a hypothesis, one or more runs, an auto-synthesized conclusion."},"663":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Experiments"},"664":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"**② Data**"},"665":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Raw sources → ordered transforms → standardized typed rows."},"666":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Data"},"667":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"**③ Algorithm**"},"668":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"One contract — `train(ctx) -> RunResult` — over any tinker-compatible backend."},"669":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Algorithms"},"670":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"**④ Evaluation**"},"671":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"A test/validation firewall: `Benchmark` (once) vs `Validation` (in-loop)."},"672":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Algorithms"},"673":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"**⑤ Extensibility**"},"674":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Eight registries — implement a protocol, register a `kind`, reference it in YAML."},"675":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Extensibility"},"676":{"id":"/docs/concepts/architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/architecture#the-five-layers","content":"Everything below this page drills into one layer. If you just want to run\nsomething, jump to the Quickstart."},"677":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","type":"page","content":"Data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/data"},"678":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"Raw sources → ordered transforms → standardized typed rows that carry only data."},"679":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"The data surface standardizes *anything* into a few typed shapes, then hands\nthose to the algorithm. Tokenization and supervision live **below** this\nboundary — the typed rows carry only data; the algorithm decides what's a\ntarget token."},"680":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"**You define:** a `DataConfig` (source + `transforms`), and a custom\n`Transform` when the built-ins don't fit. You pick which typed format the\nalgorithm consumes."},"681":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"**The SDK handles:** loading, pull/cache-by-id with lineage (`Workspace`),\nrunning transforms in order, and the strict `parse_rows` conversion."},"682":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"Class"},"683":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"Implementable?"},"684":{"id":"/docs/concepts/data-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/data","content":"Contract"},"685":{"id":"/docs/conce