concepts/extensibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#the-payoff","content":"The payoff"},"732":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","content":"The recurring pattern across the whole SDK: &#x2A;*implement a protocol → register\nit under a `kind` → reference it in YAML.** No subclassing the library, no\nfork. Researchers register their own with the same decorator in their own\nproject."},"733":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#a-registry","content":"Each extension *kind* has a `Registry(\"<kind>\")` plus `register_<kind>` /\n`get_<kind>` / `list_<kind>s` helpers."},"734":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#a-class-with-two-classvars","content":"Every implementation carries a `name` (the string used in YAML) and a `Config`\n(a Pydantic model, `extra=\"forbid\"`) — decorated with `@register_<kind>(\"<name>\")`."},"735":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#a-yaml-surface","content":"A `<Kind>Spec` model shaped as `kind` + `params`, and a `list[<Kind>Spec]`\nfield on whatever config owns it."},"736":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#a-factory","content":"Resolves specs into instances: look up the class via `get_<kind>(spec.kind)`,\nvalidate `spec.params` against the class's `Config`, then construct."},"737":{"id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#the-eight-registries","content":"One registry per extension point. The YAML `k