ts/extensibility-43","page_id":"/docs/concepts/extensibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/extensibility#the-payoff","content":"See the registry API and the\nSDK Reference for every built-in kind."},"768":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"page","content":"RL — Reinforcement Learning","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting Started","Examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl"},"769":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-0","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl","content":"A complete, run-it-yourself RL walkthrough — tasks with verifiers as the reward, the built-in rl algorithm, rollouts via Harbor, in-loop validation, and local logging."},"770":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-1","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#1-the-raw-data--tasks-you-point-the-config-at","content":"1\\. The raw data — tasks you point the config at"},"771":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-2","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#2-the-verifier-is-the-reward","content":"2\\. The verifier IS the reward"},"772":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-3","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#3-the-built-in-rl-algorithm","content":"3\\. The built-in `rl` algorithm"},"773":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-4","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"4\\. Benchmarks & validation — score it *during* training"},"774":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-5","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"5\\. Local logging — where the metrics show up"},"775":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-6","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#6-run-it","content":"6\\. Run it"},"776":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-7","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/rl#next","content":"Next"},"777":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-8","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl","content":"A full walkthrough of on-policy RL for a beginner. Unlike SFT there's no \"right\nanswer\" to copy — the model **tries**, a **verifier scores the attempt**, and the\nreward pushes the policy toward higher-scoring answers. We'll teach a model to\nsolve simple arithmetic and put the answer in `<answer></answer>`."},"778":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-9","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl","content":"Runnable in the repo at &#x2A;*`examples/rl_walkthrough/`**."},"779":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-10","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#1-the-raw-data--tasks-you-point-the-config-at","content":"RL data is a **JSONL file*&#x2A; of &#x2A;*`HarborTask`** rows. Each line is a task: an\n`instruction` (the prompt the model attempts) and a `verifier` (how to score the\nattempt):"},"780":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-11","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#1-the-raw-data--tasks-you-point-the-config-at","content":"Point the config at the file — same as SFT:"},"781":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-12","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#1-the-raw-data--tasks-you-point-the-config-at","content":"**No transform is needed here.** A row with `task_id` + `instruction` +\n`verifier` is *already* a `HarborTask`, so the SDK detects the format directly.\n(If your raw data were plain QA, you'd write a `@register_transform` that builds\nthese task dicts — same idea as SFT's `jsonl_to_chat`.)"},"782":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-13","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#2-the-verifier-is-the-reward","content":"This is the heart of RL. Each task carries an **in-process verifier**:"},"783":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-14","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#2-the-verifier-is-the-reward","content":"`fn_name` is a built-in reward function — `contains`, `exact_match`,\n`regex_match`, or `tool_calls_match`."},"784":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-15","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#2-the-verifier-is-the-reward","content":"`expected` is what it checks the model's completion for."},"785":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-16","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#2-the-verifier-is-the-reward","content":"When training runs, the policy **rolls out** on `instruction` (generates an\nanswer), and the verifier returns a reward (here: 1.0 if the completion contains\n`<answer>4</answer>`, else 0.0). That reward is the entire learning signal — no\ngold completion is ever shown to the model."},"786":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-17","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#3-the-built-in-rl-algorithm","content":"Select `rl` by `kind`. Rollouts are executed by **Harbor's engine**;\n`num_samples: 2` generates two attempts per task so the algorithm can compute a\n**group-relative advantage** (which attempt beat the other) as its baseline:"},"787":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-18","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"Exactly like SFT: a benchmark is a **directory** with a `tasks.jsonl` of\nverifier-scored tasks, attached under `metadata.benchmark` with a `run_every` so\nit's scored **in-loop every N steps**:"},"788":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-19","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"`run_every: N` scores the benchmark **in-loop every N steps**; omit `run_every`\nand it's scored **once, after training** (any entry — a `test` benchmark can run\nin-loop too). `split` (`val` / `test`) is just a label that keeps different\nbenchmarks' metrics apart in the logs; it doesn't decide when an entry runs."},"789":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-20","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"Same `local_logger` callback as everywhere:"},"790":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-21","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"It writes to `examples/rl_walkthrough/outputs/rl_arithmetic/`:"},"791":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-22","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"File"},"792":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-23","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"What's in it"},"793":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-24","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`metrics.jsonl`"},"794":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-25","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"per-step rows `{step, split, metrics}` — train rows carry `reward/mean` and friends (`split: \"train\"`); in-loop val rows carry `val/val/pass@1` (`split: \"val\"`)"},"795":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-26","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`predictions/val.jsonl`"},"796":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-27","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"the model's actual rollout for each val task"},"797":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-28","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`summary.md`"},"798":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-29","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"final status + per-eval metric lines"},"799":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-30","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"Train rows carry `reward/mean` (`split: \"train\"`); in-loop val rows carry\n`val/val/pass@1` (`split: \"val\"`). As the policy learns, you watch `reward/mean`\nrise."},"800":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-31","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#next","content":"<Card title=\"🎯 SFT walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/sft\" />"},"801":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-32","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#next","content":"<Card title=\"🎓 SDFT walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/sdft\" />"},"802":{"id":"/docs/examples/rl-33","page_id":"/docs/examples/rl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/rl#next","content":"<Card title=\"🔁 Autoresearch\" href=\"/docs/autoresearch\" />"},"803":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"page","content":"SDFT — Self-Distillation Fine-Tuning","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting Started","Examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft"},"804":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-0","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft","content":"A complete, run-it-yourself SDFT walkthrough — prompts with gold answers, a frozen teacher built from the same model, the built-in sdft algorithm, in-loop validation, and local logging."},"805":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-1","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#1-the-raw-data--prompts-you-point-the-config-at","content":"1\\. The raw data — prompts you point the config at"},"806":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-2","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"2\\. How the teacher works (no extra config)"},"807":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-3","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#3-the-built-in-sdft-algorithm","content":"3\\. The built-in `sdft` algorithm"},"808":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-4","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"4\\. Benchmarks & validation — score it *during* training"},"809":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-5","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"5\\. Local logging — where the metrics show up"},"810":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-6","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#6-run-it","content":"6\\. Run it"},"811":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-7","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sdft#next","content":"Next"},"812":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-8","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft","content":"A full walkthrough of self-distillation for a beginner. The trick: there's **no\nseparate, larger teacher model**. The same base model — shown the gold answer as\nan in-context hint — acts as the teacher, and the student is trained to match the\nteacher's *answer-aware* distribution while rolling out on its own. We'll teach a\nmodel to answer capital-city questions."},"813":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-9","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft","content":"Runnable in the repo at &#x2A;*`examples/sdft_walkthrough/`**."},"814":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-10","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#1-the-raw-data--prompts-you-point-the-config-at","content":"SDFT data is a **JSONL file*&#x2A; of &#x2A;*`PromptExample`** rows: a question and the\ngold answer the teacher (not the student) is allowed to see:"},"815":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-11","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#1-the-raw-data--prompts-you-point-the-config-at","content":"Point the config at the file:"},"816":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-12","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#1-the-raw-data--prompts-you-point-the-config-at","content":"**No transform is needed** — `{inputs: {question}, expected}` is already a\n`PromptExample`, so the SDK detects the format directly. (As always, you could\nwrite a `@register_transform` if your raw data came in a different shape.)"},"817":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-13","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"There's no teacher model to configure — it's &#x2A;*built automatically from\n`model.name`**. Each step:"},"818":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-14","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"The **student** rolls out on the question on-policy (its own current answer)."},"819":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-15","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"A frozen **teacher** — the same base model, but shown the gold `expected`\nanswer as an in-context demo — scores the rollout's **top-K** next-token\ndistribution. That's \"what a model that knew the answer would say.\""},"820":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-16","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"The student is **CE-distilled** toward that teacher distribution."},"821":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-17","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#2-how-the-teacher-works-no-extra-config","content":"`topk` controls how many teacher tokens are distilled per step. `user_template`\n(`\"{question}\"`) renders the prompt the student rolls out on."},"822":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-18","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"Identical to the other two: a benchmark **directory** with a verifier-scored\n`tasks.jsonl`, attached under `metadata.benchmark` with a `run_every` so it's\nscored **in-loop every N steps**:"},"823":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-19","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-it-during-training","content":"`run_every: N` scores the benchmark **in-loop every N steps**; omit `run_every`\nand it's scored **once, after training** (any entry — a `test` benchmark can run\nin-loop too). `split` (`val` / `test`) is just a label that keeps different\nbenchmarks' metrics apart in the logs; it doesn't decide when an entry runs."},"824":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-20","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"Same `local_logger` callback, writing to\n`examples/sdft_walkthrough/outputs/sdft_capitals/`:"},"825":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-21","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"File"},"826":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-22","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"What's in it"},"827":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-23","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`metrics.jsonl`"},"828":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-24","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"per-step rows `{step, split, metrics}` — train rows carry `train/mean_loss` (`split: \"train\"`); in-loop val rows carry `val/val/pass@1` (`split: \"val\"`)"},"829":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-25","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`predictions/val.jsonl`"},"830":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-26","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"the student's answer for each val question"},"831":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-27","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`summary.md`"},"832":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-28","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"final status + per-eval metric lines"},"833":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-29","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🎯 SFT walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/sft\" />"},"834":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-30","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🏆 RL walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/rl\" />"},"835":{"id":"/docs/examples/sdft-31","page_id":"/docs/examples/sdft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sdft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🔁 Autoresearch\" href=\"/docs/autoresearch\" />"},"836":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"page","content":"SFT — Supervised Fine-Tuning","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Getting Started","Examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft"},"837":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-0","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft","content":"A complete, run-it-yourself SFT walkthrough — JSONL data, a transform, the built-in sft algorithm, in-loop validation, and local logging, explained line by line."},"838":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-1","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#1-the-raw-data--jsonl-rows-you-point-the-config-at","content":"1\\. The raw data — JSONL rows you point the config at"},"839":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-2","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"2\\. The transform — shape raw rows into a chat conversation"},"840":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-3","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#3-the-built-in-sft-algorithm","content":"3\\. The built-in `sft` algorithm"},"841":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-4","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"4\\. Benchmarks & validation — score the model *during* training"},"842":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-5","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"5\\. Local logging — where the metrics show up"},"843":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-6","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#6-run-it","content":"6\\. Run it"},"844":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-7","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/examples/sft#next","content":"Next"},"845":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-8","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft","content":"This is a full walkthrough for someone who has never used the SDK. We'll train a\nsmall model to pick the right tool for a user's query — emitting\n`<answer>TOOL_SLUG</answer>` — and explain **every** moving part: the raw data,\nthe transform that shapes it, the built-in algorithm, in-loop validation, and\nwhere the logs land."},"846":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-9","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft","content":"Everything here is a real, runnable example in the repo at\n&#x2A;*`examples/sft_walkthrough/`**. You can run it directly (see step 6)."},"847":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-10","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#1-the-raw-data--jsonl-rows-you-point-the-config-at","content":"Training data is a **JSONL file**: one JSON object per line. You bring whatever\nshape your data is in — here, each line is a query and the tool that answers it:"},"848":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-11","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#1-the-raw-data--jsonl-rows-you-point-the-config-at","content":"You don't load this yourself. You **point the config at the file** — `source_kind:\njsonl` tells the SDK it's a JSONL file, and `path` is where to find it (relative\nto where you run from, or absolute):"},"849":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-12","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#1-the-raw-data--jsonl-rows-you-point-the-config-at","content":"The SDK reads the file through a **data store** and hands the rows to the next\nstage. At this point they're still raw dicts — `{\"query\": ..., \"tool_slug\": ...}`."},"850":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-13","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"An algorithm doesn't train on arbitrary dicts. SFT trains on a\n&#x2A;*`ChatMessagesRow`** — a conversation of `{role, content}` messages. A\n**transform** bridges the two."},"851":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-14","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"A transform is just a function with one contract: &#x2A;*`rows -> rows`**. You list\ntransforms in the config and they run in order. The built-in `jsonl_to_chat`\nrenders each raw dict into a chat turn using templates you provide:"},"852":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-15","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"So this raw row:"},"853":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-16","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"becomes this `ChatMessagesRow`:"},"854":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-17","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"The conversation carries **only data** — it does *not* say which tokens to learn\nfrom. That's the algorithm's decision (next step)."},"855":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-18","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"When no built-in fits, write your own and reference it by `kind` — no SDK fork:"},"856":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-19","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#2-the-transform--shape-raw-rows-into-a-chat-conversation","content":"Then add `{ kind: strip_pii, params: { field: query } }` to `transforms`. The\nSDK finds it in the registry by that name. See Extensibility."},"857":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-20","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#3-the-built-in-sft-algorithm","content":"You don't implement training — you select a built-in algorithm by `kind` and\npass its knobs. `sft&#x60; tokenizes each chat row (masking the loss to the assistant\nturns) and runs the SDK training loop on the hosted &#x2A;*`tinker`** backend:"},"858":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-21","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#3-the-built-in-sft-algorithm","content":"`supervise: all_assistant` is what makes this *supervised* — the loss is on the\nassistant tokens (the `<answer>…</answer>`), not the prompt. Note this lives on\nthe **algorithm**, not the data: the same chat rows could be used differently by\nanother algorithm."},"859":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-22","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"To know if training is working, you score the model against a held-out\n**benchmark** while it trains. A benchmark is a **directory** containing a\n`tasks.jsonl` — each task has an `instruction` (the full prompt) and a\n**verifier** that says whether an answer is correct:"},"860":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-23","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"You attach it under `metadata.benchmark&#x60; and give it a &#x2A;*`run_every`** so it's\nscored **in-loop, repeatedly, every N steps**:"},"861":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-24","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"Two **independent** knobs to understand:"},"862":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-25","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"**`run_every` controls *when* it's scored.** `run_every: N` scores the\nbenchmark **in-loop every N steps** during training; omit `run_every` and it's\nscored **once, after training**. (This is true of any entry — a `test`\nbenchmark can have a `run_every` and run in-loop too.)"},"863":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-26","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#4-benchmarks--validation--score-the-model-during-training","content":"**`split` (`val` / `test`) is just a label** — it namespaces the metrics so\ndifferent benchmarks' scores stay apart in the logs; it does *not* decide when\nan entry runs. `pass@1` here = the fraction of tasks whose answer the verifier\naccepts (contains the right `<answer>SLUG</answer>`)."},"864":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-27","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"Logging is a **callback** on the experiment. `local_logger` prints a per-step\nline and writes the metrics to disk:"},"865":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-28","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"It writes to &#x2A;*`<output_dir>/<run_name>/`**, which the runner sets to\n`examples/sft_walkthrough/outputs/sft_tool_selection/`:"},"866":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-29","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"File"},"867":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-30","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"What's in it"},"868":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-31","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`metrics.jsonl`"},"869":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-32","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"one row per event — `{step, split, metrics}`. **Train** steps are tagged `split: \"train\"`; the in-loop **validation** scores are tagged `split: \"val\"` (so you can tell them apart)."},"870":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-33","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`predictions/val.jsonl`"},"871":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-34","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"the model's actual answer for each val task each time it's scored"},"872":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-35","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"`summary.md`"},"873":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-36","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"final status + the per-eval metric lines, written at the end"},"874":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-37","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"A typical `metrics.jsonl` looks like:"},"875":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-38","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"Each row is `{step, split, metrics}` — training steps are tagged\n`split: \"train\"` and the in-loop validation scores are tagged `split: \"val\"`, so\nboth live in one file:"},"876":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-39","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#5-local-logging--where-the-metrics-show-up","content":"You read training loss and validation score side by side, scored in-loop."},"877":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-40","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#6-run-it","content":"Everything above is the file `examples/sft_walkthrough/config.yaml`. The runner\njust loads it and calls the SDK:"},"878":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-41","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#6-run-it","content":"The runner uses `Experiment(cfg).run()` (not the bare `run_experiment`) so the\n`local_logger` callback fires and writes the files above — including\n`experiment.md` with the hypothesis and conclusion."},"879":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-42","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#6-run-it","content":"You get a LoRA adapter that emits the tool slug, plus the `metrics.jsonl` /\n`predictions/` / `summary.md` from step 5. Bump `max_steps` and grow the val set\nfor a run that actually moves the needle."},"880":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-43","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🏆 RL walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/rl\" />"},"881":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-44","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🎓 SDFT walkthrough\" href=\"/docs/examples/sdft\" />"},"882":{"id":"/docs/examples/sft-45","page_id":"/docs/examples/sft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/examples/sft#next","content":"<Card title=\"🔁 Autoresearch\" href=\"/docs/autoresearch\" />"},"883":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","type":"page","content":"evsys_sdk","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk"},"884":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#oop-orchestration","content":"OOP orchestration"},"885":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#config-models","content":"Config models"},"886":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#yaml","content":"YAML"},"887":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#registries-decorators-for-ext