/>"},"926":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-42","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/training&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;training&#x22;\" />"},"927":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-43","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/backends&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;backends&#x22;\" />"},"928":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-44","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;algorithms&#x22;\" />"},"929":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-45","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/verifiers&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;verifiers&#x22;\" />"},"930":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-46","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/transforms&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;transforms&#x22;\" />"},"931":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-47","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/log_stores&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;log_stores&#x22;\" />"},"932":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-48","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/inference&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;inference&#x22;\" />"},"933":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk-49","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk#imperative-runner-kept-for-advanced-use-experiment-is-the-default","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/eval&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;eval&#x22;\" />"},"934":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","type":"page","content":"Agents","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents"},"935":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","content":"The pluggable rollout harness the policy is trained inside, so it learns to use that harness."},"936":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"937":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"938":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"939":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"940":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","content":"An **agent** is the rollout harness for RL (and SDFT) — the harbor `BaseAgent`\nthat actually drives the model through a task, turn by turn, and records what\nhappened. It's pluggable on purpose: point at any harbor agent and the model\ntrains *inside* that harness, so it learns to use it. This is the same principle\nas Opus being trained inside the Claude Code harness — the policy adapts to the\nexact loop, tools, and message flow it will run under at inference time. You'd\nwrite your own to train against a multi-turn loop, a tool-use protocol, or a\ncustom environment."},"941":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"The default harness is `BasicLoopAgent` in\n`src/evsys_sdk/training/harbor_agents.py`. It subclasses `BaseAgent` from\n`harbor.agents.base`, which the rollout engine builds fresh per trial. The\nmethods a harbor `BaseAgent` implements (as `BasicLoopAgent` shows):"},"942":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"**`@staticmethod name() -> str`** — the agent's harbor name\n(`\"evsys-basic-loop\"`). A static method returning a string."},"943":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"**`version(self) -> str | None`** — an optional version string (`\"1.0.0\"`)."},"944":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"**`async setup(self, environment: BaseEnvironment) -> None`** — one-time prep\nbefore any rollout, given the environment harbor allocated (the SDK default is\n`NoOpEnvironment`, a sandbox-free in-process env). Returns nothing."},"945":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"**`async run(self, instruction: str, environment: BaseEnvironment, context: AgentContext) -> None`**\nThe core method — one rollout for one task. This is what you override."},"946":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"`instruction` — the task prompt (the templated `HarborTask.instruction`)."},"947":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"`environment` — the harbor environment to act in (exec/upload/download;\nno-op for in-process runs)."},"948":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"`context: AgentContext` — the object harbor harvests after the rollout. The\nagent **writes its results onto it**: `BasicLoopAgent` sets\n`context.rollout_details` (token-level data — present for tinker, empty for\nAPI models), plus `context.n_input_tokens`, `context.n_output_tokens`,\n`context.n_cache_tokens`, and `context.cost_usd` (usage/cost, harbor records\nthese on the trial). It also writes the completion text to its agent dir so\nthe host-side verifier can read and score it."},"949":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"Returns nothing — all output flows through `context` and the agent dir."},"950":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#the-contract","content":"`BasicLoopAgent.run` drives a `Chat(<llm>)` for `max_turns` turns. Its `__init__`\ntakes the kwargs the RL/SDFT engine passes through: `model_name`, `model_path`,\n`renderer_name`, `max_tokens`, `temperature`, `max_turns`, `system_prompt`,\n`model_client`, `api_base`. `model_client` picks the sampler: `\"tinker\"` (an\non-policy `TinkerLLM` reading the just-saved `model_path` — this is the path the\ngradient flows back through) or `\"litellm\"` (any litellm provider, for\nbenchmarking closed/API models through the same harness)."},"951":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"There's one built-in harness; you select an alternative by pointing the RL\nalgorithm at any harbor agent's import path:"},"952":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"When `agent_import_path` is `null`, the engine uses\n`BasicLoopAgent`, parameterized by the rollout kwargs above. When you set it to a\n`\"module.path:ClassName\"` string, **that agent wins and the engine passes it no\nkwargs** — it must be fully self-configured."},"953":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"954":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"955":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"`BasicLoopAgent` (`evsys-basic-loop`)"},"956":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#use-a-built-in","content":"Drives `Chat(TinkerLLM(model_path))` for `max_turns` turns on the current policy weights, records token-level `rollout_details` + usage/cost onto the `AgentContext`, and writes the completion for the host-side verifier. Switch `model_client` to `\"litellm\"` to benchmark an API model through the same path."},"957":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#create-your-own","content":"A custom harness is any harbor `BaseAgent` whose `run` drives your loop and\nwrites the rollout onto the `AgentContext`:"},"958":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#create-your-own","content":"Because the engine hands a self-configured agent no kwargs, give your `__init__`\nthe defaults it needs to construct a sampler on the current policy."},"959":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"A custom agent ships as an ordinary Python class — the RL config references it by\nits `module.path:ClassName` import string, so any installed package (or your own\nproject module) works with no SDK fork. The engine imports it by that path at\nrollout time, exactly as it imports the built-in `BasicLoopAgent`."},"960":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Algorithms\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms\" />"},"961":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Backends\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends\" />"},"962":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"963":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"page","content":"Algorithms","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms"},"964":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","content":"The training recipe — SFT, RL, distillation, or any custom loss — that decides what each batch contains."},"965":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"966":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"The easy path: `BaseAlgorithm`"},"967":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"`TrainingBatch` — where the loss lives"},"968":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"969":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"970":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"971":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","content":"An **algorithm** is a training recipe. It owns one thing the rest of the stack\ndoes not: *how each step's batch is built and which loss it trains under*.\nEverything else — backend allocation, step/save cadence, evaluators, logging,\nartifacts — is shared plumbing. **Any** algorithm is supported (LoRA on any\nmodel, any loss) by overriding a single method, so you write your own whenever\nthe recipe differs from SFT/RL/SDFT."},"972":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"At the protocol level (`src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py`), an algorithm declares two\nClassVars and implements one method:"},"973":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key and the YAML `algorithm.kind`."},"974":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model for the recipe's params,\nvalidated against `algorithm.params` in YAML."},"975":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"**`train(self, ctx: RunContext) -> RunResult`** — execute one full run."},"976":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"`ctx: RunContext` carries everything the run needs: `run_id`, `output_dir`,\n`config` (the parsed `ExperimentConfig`), `data_store`, `log_store`,\n`backend`, and a free-form `extras` dict (where the backend handles, the\n`train_rows`, the `model_name`, etc. live)."},"977":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-contract","content":"**Returns** a `RunResult`: `run_id`, `status` (`\"completed\"`/`\"failed\"`/\n`\"cancelled\"`), `metrics` (final scalars), `artifacts` (named paths, e.g.\n`{\"run_dir\": ..., \"checkpoint-final\": ...}`), and an optional `error` string."},"978":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"The Tinker-backed recipes don't reimplement `train`. They subclass\n`BaseAlgorithm` (`src/evsys_sdk/algorithms/base.py`), which owns the whole\ncomposer body and **is itself the StepBuilder** the loop drives. A concrete\nalgorithm overrides just the per-recipe pieces:"},"979":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"**`async setup(self, ctx: RunContext, backend: TinkerBackend) -> None`**\nOne-time prep before the loop. Stash per-algorithm state on `self` (tokenized\ndatums for SFT; dataset + teacher client for SDFT/RL) and &#x2A;*must set\n`self._steps_per_epoch`**. The `backend` is the already-allocated LoRA\ntraining client; call `backend.get_tokenizer()`, `backend.save_for_sampler(...)`,\netc. Returns nothing."},"980":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"**`async build_batch(self, step_idx: int) -> TrainingBatch`**\nProduce the batch for `step_idx` (0-based). SFT slices its static datums; RL\nand SDFT roll out **on-policy** here. &#x2A;*The loss rides on the returned batch —\nthere is no separate loss override.** Returns a `TrainingBatch`."},"981":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"**`step_metrics(self, step_idx: int, batch: TrainingBatch, fb_result: Any) -> dict[str, float]`*&#x2A;\n&#x2A;(Optional, defaults to `{}`.)* Per-step metrics computed from the\nforward-backward result. `fb_result` is what the backend's\n`forward_backward_*_async()` future resolved to; inspect\n`fb_result.loss_fn_outputs` (one entry per Datum) to derive, e.g., `train_mean_nll`."},"982":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#the-easy-path-basealgorithm","content":"`BaseAlgorithmConfig` supplies the shared knobs every recipe inherits\n(`extra=\"forbid\"`): `learning_rate`, `num_epochs`, `batch_size`, `max_steps`\n(a hard cap that wins over `num_epochs * steps_per_epoch`), `lora_rank`,\n`renderer_name`, `enable_thinking`, `save_every` / `save_at_fractions`,\n`callbacks`, and Adam knobs. A subclass adds its own and may re-declare a field\nto change its default (RL drops `learning_rate` to `1e-5`)."},"983":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"From `src/evsys_sdk/training/loop.py`, the dataclass `build_batch` returns:"},"984":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"**`data: list[tinker.Datum]`** — the step's training examples. The loss mask on\neach Datum decides which tokens are supervised (the algorithm's call, not the\ndataset's)."},"985":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"**`loss_fn: tinker.types.LossFnType | LossCallable`** — *either* a\nserver-recognized string name (`\"cross_entropy\"`, `\"importance_sampling\"`, …)\nfor a server-side loss, *or* a Python callable for a client-side custom loss.\nThe loop dispatches the right backend method based on the type:\n`forward_backward_async` for a string, `forward_backward_custom_async` for a\ncallable. A `LossCallable` is `Callable[[model_output, batch_metadata], Any]`\nreturning a scalar tensor for the backward pass."},"986":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"**`loss_fn_config: dict[str, Any] | None`** — extra loss params; only used when\n`loss_fn` is a string."},"987":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"**`metrics: dict[str, float]`** — algorithm-precomputed per-step metrics (e.g.\nreward stats, teacher entropy) merged into the per-step log row."},"988":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#trainingbatch--where-the-loss-lives","content":"This is the seam for **any loss**: focal loss, DPO, GRPO, a custom RL objective —\noverride `build_batch`, set the `loss_fn`, and the shared loop drives it."},"989":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"990":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"991":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`sft`"},"992":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"Supervised fine-tuning on Tinker. Tokenizes chat rows to static datums with assistant-span masks; `loss_fn=\"cross_entropy\"`. Knobs: `max_seq_len`, `supervise`."},"993":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`rl`"},"994":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"On-policy RL on Tinker. Rolls out the batch through harbor's Job engine, group-normalizes advantages, emits `loss_fn=\"importance_sampling\"` Datums. Knobs: `num_samples`, `verifier_name`, `agent_import_path`, `n_concurrent`."},"995":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`sdft`"},"996":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"Self-distillation FT on Tinker. On-policy student rollout → frozen-teacher top-K scoring → `cross_entropy` soft-target distillation. Knobs: `topk`, `max_context_length`, `demo_template`."},"997":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`local_sft`"},"998":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-34","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"TRL `SFTTrainer` on the `local` backend (transformers + peft + trl). LoRA on any HF model, runs on CPU/MPS/CUDA."},"999":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-35","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`local_rl`"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-36","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"TRL `GRPOTrainer` on the `local` backend, reward driven by a registered verifier (`verifier_kind` / `verifier_params`)."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-37","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"`mock_sft`"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-38","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#use-a-built-in","content":"Fake SFT for tests: logs a deterministic loss curve and writes stub checkpoints. No backend needed."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-39","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#create-your-own","content":"Subclass a concrete recipe and override one method — here, SFT with a custom\nclient-side loss:"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-40","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#create-your-own","content":"For a recipe built from scratch, subclass `BaseAlgorithm` instead and implement\n`setup` + `build_batch` (+ optionally `step_metrics`)."},"1005":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-41","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"A third-party package self-registers via a Python entry point in the\n`evsys_sdk.algorithms` group:"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-42","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Importing `evsys_sdk` imports the target module, running its `@register_algorithm`\ndecorator — the recipe is selectable by name from any `config.yaml`, no SDK fork."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-43","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Backends\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends\" />"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-44","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Agents\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents\" />"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms-45","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","type":"page","content":"Backends","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","content":"The compute plane that materializes a model and hands training resources to the algorithm."},"1012":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","content":"A **backend** is the seam between an algorithm and the machine that runs it. Its\none job is to materialize a model plus its training resources (a client, a\ntokenizer, a service handle) and pass them along so the algorithm stays\nhardware-agnostic. You'd write your own to put the SDK on any **Tinker-compatible**\ntraining server — anything that exposes the Tinker training-server API, such as\nFireworks, TML, or SkyRL — without touching algorithm code."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"A backend is any class satisfying the `Backend` protocol in\n`src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py`. It declares one ClassVar and implements two methods:"},"1018":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key, also the string you write under\n`backend.kind` in YAML (`\"tinker\"`, `\"local\"`, `\"mock\"`)."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model (`extra=\"forbid\"`) describing\nthe backend's params. Whatever you put under `backend.params` in YAML is\nvalidated against this before the backend is constructed."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"**`prepare(self, *, model: dict[str, Any], run_dir: str) -> dict[str, Any]`**\nCalled once before training. Both arguments are keyword-only."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"`model` — a dict describing the model to fine-tune. It carries at least\n`model[\"name\"]` (the HuggingFace identifier), and optionally\n`model[\"load_checkpoint_path\"]`, `model[\"init_from_checkpoint\"]`, and\n`model[\"renderer_name\"]` (these come straight from the YAML `model:` block)."},"1022":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"`run_dir` — the local filesystem directory this run may write to."},"1023":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"**Returns** a dict of backend-specific *handles* that the runner attaches to\n`ctx.extras[\"backend_handles\"]`. The algorithm reads from it — e.g. a tinker\nrun needs `{\"backend\": \"tinker\", \"service_client\": ..., \"model_name\": ...,\n\"renderer_name\": ..., \"run_dir\": ...}`; a local run needs\n`{\"model\": <hf_model>, \"tokenizer\": ..., ...}`. The keys are a private\ncontract between a backend and the algorithms that target it."},"1024":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"**`teardown(self, handles: dict[str, Any]) -> None`**\nCalled once after training to release whatever `prepare` allocated. `handles`\nis exactly the dict `prepare` returned. Returns nothing. (`MockBackend` and\n`TinkerBackend` no-op here; `LocalBackend` drops the model and empties the\nCUDA/MPS cache.)"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#the-contract","content":"The `Algorithm` protocol is deliberately *not* parameterized by `Backend`. The\nregistry routes a `(recipe.kind, backend.kind)` pair to a concrete algorithm\ninstead, so a backend never knows which recipe will run against it."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"`tinker`"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"Creates a `tinker.ServiceClient` (Tinker-compatible server); returns it plus `model_name` and checkpoint/renderer hints. The real LoRA training client is allocated later by the algorithm. Reads the API key from `api_key_env` (default `TINKER_API_KEY`); `base_url` overrides the service URL."},"1030":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"`local`"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"Loads an HF tokenizer + `AutoModelForCausalLM` via transformers; returns the model + tokenizer for the TRL-based `local_*` algorithms. Params: `dtype` (`bfloat16`/`float16`/`float32`), `device` (`auto`/`cpu`/`cuda`/`mps`), `trust_remote_code`."},"1032":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"`mock`"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#use-a-built-in","content":"Deterministic, no I/O. `prepare` returns a stub dict; `teardown` is a no-op. For tests. Param `fail_on_prepare` forces `prepare` to raise."},"1034":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"A third-party package self-registers via a Python entry point in the\n`evsys_sdk.backends` group:"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Importing `evsys_sdk` walks that group and imports the target module, running its\n`@register_backend` decorator — your backend is available by name with no SDK fork."},"1036":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Algorithms\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/algorithms\" />"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Agents\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/agents\" />"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/backends#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"page","content":"Callbacks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","content":"Lifecycle + logging hooks fired through the experiment and training loop."},"1041":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1042":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"What `local_logger` writes, exactly"},"1044":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","content":"A **callback** is an object that gets called at fixed moments — when the\nexperiment starts, before/after each run, after every training step, on each\neval, on checkpoint, at the end. Callbacks are how logging, dashboards,\nprogress printing, and early stopping plug in without touching the loop. You\nlist them on `ExperimentConfig.callbacks`; you write your own when you need a\nside effect (ship to S3, push to a service, stop early) the built-ins don't\ncover."},"1047":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","content":"Two safety properties matter: **a raising callback never kills the run** (the\nexception is logged at WARNING and the next callback runs), and **every hook has\na no-op default** so you override only the ones you care about."},"1048":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"The base class is `evsys_sdk.training.callbacks.Callback`. There is no `Config`\nrequirement on the base, but built-ins carry `name` + `Config` ClassVars so they\nwork from YAML. Two kinds of state object are threaded in:"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`LogState`** (called `LoopState` in code) — live training-loop state:\n`.step`, `.num_steps`, `.output_dir`, `.backend`, `.log_store`,\n`.checkpoint_mgr`, `.stop_requested`, `.ctx`. Call `state.request_stop()` from\nany loop hook to break the loop after the current step finishes."},"1050":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`LogContext`** — experiment-wide context shared across all hooks:\n`.output_dir`, `.config`, `.store`, `.run_key`, `.run_config`, `.group_name`,\n`.ids` (dashboard ids populated by logger callbacks), `.extras` (scratch shared\nbetween callbacks within a run)."},"1051":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"Here is **every hook**, with its exact signature and when it fires."},"1052":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**Loop-scope hooks** (dispatched by the `TrainingLoop`):"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_train_start(self, state: LoopState) -> None`** — once, before the for-loop\nstarts. Open log files, init a wandb run, snapshot config."},"1054":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_step_end(self, state: LoopState, step_idx: int, batch: TrainingBatch, metrics: dict[str, float]) -> None`**\n— after every train step's metric row is written. `step_idx` is the 0-based\nstep; `batch` is the step's training batch; `metrics` is that step's metric\ndict. The universal per-step hook."},"1055":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_eval(self, state: LoopState, step_idx: int, eval_name: str, metrics: dict[str, float]) -> None`**\n— once per evaluator after each in-loop eval. `eval_name` identifies the\nevaluator; `metrics` is its scalar output. Drives early stopping and val curves."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_checkpoint(self, state: LoopState, row: ManifestRow) -> None`** — after each\ncheckpoint manifest row is recorded. `row` carries the checkpoint's name,\nstep, and paths. Useful for shipping/pruning checkpoints."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_train_end(self, state: LoopState, artifacts: LoopArtifacts) -> None`** —\nonce after the loop completes (including the final checkpoint save).\n`artifacts` carries totals (requested steps, train seconds, run dir,\ncheckpoints). Flush summaries, close files."},"1058":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**Experiment-scope hooks** (dispatched by the `Experiment`, not the loop — these\nlet one logger own the full lifecycle, threading dashboard ids through\n`ctx.ids`):"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_experiment_start(self, ctx: LogContext) -> None`** — once at experiment\nstart, before any arm. A logger creates the experiment record here and sets\n`ctx.ids['experiment_id']`."},"1060":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_group_start(self, ctx: LogContext, group_name: str) -> None`** — when a new\nrun-group is needed (`n_repeats` replicates or continual stages). A logger\ncreates the group → `ctx.ids[f'group:{group_name}']`."},"1061":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_run_start(self, ctx: LogContext) -> None`** — per arm, before training.\n`ctx.run_config` is set. A logger opens its run-scoped sink (e.g. `wandb.init`)\n→ `ctx.ids['run_id']`, reading the parent ids to link it."},"1062":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_benchmark_eval(self, ctx: LogContext, eval_result: EvalResult, predictions: list[dict], *, step: int | None = None) -> None`**\n— per benchmark scored, in-loop (`step` = the train step) or post-training\n(`step=None`). `eval_result` carries metrics + breakdowns + tags; `predictions`\nis the per-task prediction rows. `step` is **keyword-only**."},"1063":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_run_end(self, ctx: LogContext, run_result: RunResult, arm: ArmResult) -> None`**\n— per arm, after eval, before the run is marked completed. `run_result` is the\nalgorithm's result; `arm` is the arm record. Loggers close their sink and\nrecord final status here."},"1064":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#the-contract","content":"**`on_experiment_end(self, ctx: LogContext, result: ExperimentResult) -> None`** —\nonce at experiment end. `result` carries `best_arm`, `best_score`, `status`,\n`conclusion`. Final summary / flush."},"1065":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does / where it writes"},"1067":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`print_progress`"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Compact one-liner per step to stdout. Params: `every` (print every Nth step), `keys` (restrict printed metric keys)."},"1069":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`csv_metrics`"},"1070":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Mirrors per-step metric writes into a CSV next to `metrics.jsonl`. Params: `out_path` (parent created if missing), `delimiter` (default `,`). New metric keys append columns."},"1071":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`early_stopping`"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Watches a metric on `on_eval` and calls `state.request_stop()` after N evals without improvement. Params: `metric`, `eval_name` (or `None` = any), `patience` (default 3), `mode` (`max`/`min`), `min_delta`."},"1073":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`wandb_logger`"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-34","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"One Weights & Biases run per arm (opened `on_run_start`, closed `on_run_end`). Logs per-step + eval + benchmark metrics and a predictions `wandb.Table`. wandb is imported lazily; if missing, every hook no-ops. Surfaces the run URL on `ctx.extras['wandb_url']`. Params: `project`, `entity`, `name`, `mode`, `log_every`, `max_pred_rows`."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-35","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`tensorboard_logger`"},"1076":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-36","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"One TensorBoard event dir per arm. Logs scalar + eval + benchmark metrics via `SummaryWriter`. Lazy torch import; no-ops if missing. Params: `log_dir` (default `<output_dir>/tb/<run_key>`), `flush_secs`."},"1077":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-37","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`local_logger`"},"1078":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-38","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Human-readable local mirror — see exact outputs below."},"1079":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-39","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`evsys_logger`"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-40","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"\"Callbacks own the store\" mode: persists experiment/group/run records, per-step metrics, checkpoints, benchmark evals + predictions to the evsys dashboard, keyed off `ctx.ids`. Disables itself if the `Experiment` already has a `store=` (to avoid double-writes). Params: `project_id`, `flush_every`."},"1081":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-41","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"`debug_logger`"},"1082":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-42","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#use-a-built-in","content":"Pretty-prints every hook and its arguments to stdout — pure introspection, no persistence. Drop it in to see exactly what each logger callback receives and in what order. Params: `max_len`, `max_pred_rows`."},"1083":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-43","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"`LocalLoggerCallback` both prints a per-step one-liner (cadence `print_every`,\n`0` = silent) and persists files:"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-44","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"**`<output_dir>/<run_key>/metrics.jsonl`** — appended on every `on_step_end`\n(split `\"train\"`) and `on_eval` (split `\"val\"`). Each row is\n`{step, split, metrics}`."},"1085":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-45","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"**`<output_dir>/<run_key>/predictions/<name>.jsonl`** — written per benchmark in\n`on_benchmark_eval` when predictions are present (`<name>` is the eval name,\nslashes/spaces sanitized), one prediction row per line."},"1086":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-46","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"**`<output_dir>/<run_key>/summary.md`** — written at `on_run_end`: the run key,\nthe hypothesis (echoed in the header), final status, and one line per benchmark\neval with its metrics."},"1087":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-47","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#what-local_logger-writes-exactly","content":"**`<output_dir>/experiment.md`** — the experiment-level mirror: the hypothesis\n(read from `ctx.config.metadata['hypothesis']` at `on_experiment_start`) and\nthe conclusion (from `ExperimentResult.conclusion` at `on_experiment_end`). So\nthe local mirror carries hypothesis + conclusion even with no dashboard."},"1088":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-48","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#create-your-own","content":"Subclass `Callback`, override only the hooks you need, carry `name` + `Config`,\nand decorate with `@register_callback(\"<name>\")`:"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-49","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#create-your-own","content":"Then list it on the experiment:"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-50","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Callbacks are constructed from `{kind, params}` specs via `build_callbacks`,\nwhich validates `params` against your `Config` and resolves `kind` through the\ncallback registry. To distribute a callback without copying code, import the\nmodule that runs your `@register_callback` decorator at startup (e.g. from your\nproject's package `__init__`). Note callbacks are **not** among the entry-point\ngroups `evsys_sdk` auto-loads (those cover algorithms, verifiers, metrics, data\nstores, log stores, backends, inference, transforms) — so ensure your\nregistering module is imported before the experiment runs."},"1091":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-51","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Log stores\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores\" />"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-52","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Inference clients\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference\" />"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks-53","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","type":"page","content":"Data stores","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","content":"The read/write layer — where the SDK reads inputs from and writes outputs to."},"1096":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1098":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1099":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1100":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","content":"A **data store** is the SDK's abstract file layer: every time an algorithm reads\na dataset or writes rendered rows / predictions, it goes through a `DataStore`.\nThe default is your local filesystem, so you rarely think about it — you make\nyour own when data lives somewhere else (a database, object storage, an\nin-process cache for tests)."},"1101":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"The contract is `evsys_sdk.protocols.DataStore` (a `typing.Protocol`, so you\nsatisfy it by implementing the methods — no subclassing). An implementation\ndeclares one ClassVar and six methods:"},"1102":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key, the string you put in YAML as\n`kind`. (Data stores have no `Config` ClassVar requirement in the protocol,\nbut the built-ins carry one — see below.)"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`read_jsonl(self, path: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]`** — read a JSONL file\nat `path` and return its rows as a list of dicts, one dict per line. This is\nthe primary way datasets are loaded."},"1104":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`write_jsonl(self, path: str, rows: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]) -> None`** —\nwrite an iterable of dicts to `path`, one JSON object per line. Used for\nrendered training data, predictions, and other row-shaped outputs. Returns\nnothing."},"1105":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`read_json(self, path: str) -> Any`** — read a single JSON document at\n`path` and return the parsed value (any JSON type — dict, list, scalar)."},"1106":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`write_json(self, path: str, value: Any) -> None`** — serialize `value` to\nJSON and write it to `path`. Used for manifests, summaries, config snapshots."},"1107":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`exists(self, path: str) -> bool`** — return `True` if something is present\nat `path`, `False` otherwise. Callers use this to skip work or guard reads."},"1108":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#the-contract","content":"**`list(self, prefix: str) -> list[str]`** — return the paths under `prefix`.\nFor the local store, a directory prefix is walked recursively and a glob\npattern is expanded; paths come back relative to the store root."},"1109":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"The local filesystem store is the default; you almost never name it explicitly.\nWhen you do, it looks like this:"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does / where it writes"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`local`"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`LocalDataStore` (`src/evsys_sdk/data_stores/local.py`). Reads/writes JSONL and JSON on the filesystem, no network. Relative `path`s resolve against `root` (default `\".\"`); absolute paths pass through. `write_*` create parent dirs; `list` walks a directory recursively or expands a glob, returning paths relative to `root`."},"1114":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`in_memory`"},"1115":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`InMemoryDataStore` (`src/evsys_sdk/data_stores/in_memory.py`). Keeps JSONL and JSON in two dicts keyed by path — nothing touches disk. `read_*` raise `FileNotFoundError` for unknown paths. For tests."},"1116":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#create-your-own","content":"Implement the six methods, carry `name` + a `Config` Pydantic model\n(`extra=\"forbid\"` so YAML typos fail loudly), and decorate with\n`@register_data_store(\"<name>\")`:"},"1117":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#create-your-own","content":"Then reference it by `kind` in YAML — no SDK edit:"},"1118":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"To make your store importable from any project without copying code, expose it\nas a Python entry point under the group `evsys_sdk.data_stores` in your\npackage's `pyproject.toml`:"},"1119":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"On import, `evsys_sdk` walks that group and imports the target, running its\n`@register_data_store` decorator — your `kind` is available everywhere with no\nfork."},"1120":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Log stores\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores\" />"},"1121":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Inference clients\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference\" />"},"1122":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1123":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","type":"page","content":"Inference clients","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference"},"1124":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","content":"How evaluation and RL query a model to generate text."},"1125":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1126":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1127":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1128":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1129":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","content":"An **inference client** is the thing that turns a prompt into generated text.\nEvaluators call it to produce predictions; RL rollouts call it to sample\ncompletions. The SDK ships clients for local HF models, Tinker, and the\nfrontier APIs (Claude, OpenAI, Gemini). You make your own to wrap any model or\nendpoint behind the same one-method contract."},"1130":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"The contract is `evsys_sdk.protocols.InferenceClient` (a `typing.Protocol`). It\ndeclares one ClassVar and one method:"},"1131":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key / YAML `kind`."},"1132":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"**`generate(self, *, prompt: str, max_tokens: int = 256, temperature: float = 0.0, stop: list[str] | None = None) -> str`**\n— synchronously generate text and return it as a string. **All arguments are\nkeyword-only** (note the leading `*`):"},"1133":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"`prompt` — the input text to generate from."},"1134":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"`max_tokens` — cap on generated tokens (default `256`)."},"1135":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"`temperature` — sampling temperature; `0.0` (default) means greedy/deterministic."},"1136":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"`stop` — optional list of stop strings; generation is truncated at the first\none that appears (`None` = no stop strings)."},"1137":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#the-contract","content":"The return is the generated completion as a plain `str`."},"1138":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"Or a real API client:"},"1139":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1140":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does / where it writes"},"1141":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`mock`"},"1142":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`MockInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/mock.py`). Returns a fixed `template` for every call (the `{prompt}` placeholder is filled in), honoring `stop`. Deterministic; for tests. Default template is `<think>mock thinking</think>\\n<answer>MOCK_ANSWER</answer>`."},"1143":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`local`"},"1144":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`LocalInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/local.py`). Generates from a local HuggingFace causal LM (`transformers`/`torch`). Params: `model_name`, optional `adapter_path` (PEFT/LoRA), `dtype` (`bfloat16`/`float16`/`float32`), `device`. Sampling on when `temperature > 0`."},"1145":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`tinker`"},"1146":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`TinkerInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/tinker.py`). Generates via the Tinker sampling client. Optional dep — registers only if `tinker` is importable."},"1147":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`claude`"},"1148":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`ClaudeInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/claude.py`). Anthropic Messages API; needs the `anthropic` package and an API key from `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (env var name configurable). Sends `prompt` as one user message; optional `system_prompt`. Params include `model`, `base_url`, `default_max_tokens`, `timeout_s`, `extra_headers`."},"1149":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`openai`"},"1150":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`OpenAIInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/openai.py`). OpenAI Chat Completions; needs `openai` and `OPENAI_API_KEY`. `base_url` can point at any compatible endpoint (vLLM, Together). Params: `model`, `organization`, `system_prompt`, `timeout_s`."},"1151":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`gemini`"},"1152":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`GeminiInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/gemini.py`). Google `google-genai` SDK; key from `GEMINI_API_KEY` (falls back to `GOOGLE_API_KEY`). Params: `model`, `system_instruction`."},"1153":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`chat_templated`"},"1154":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#use-a-built-in","content":"`ChatTemplatedInference` (`src/evsys_sdk/inference/chat_templated.py`). A **wrapper**, not a standalone client: it rebuilds a (system + user) chat template around the raw prompt before forwarding to a base client, so eval-time inputs match the chat-templated distribution a model was SFT'd on. Requires the base client to expose a `_tokenizer`. Not registered as a `kind`."},"1155":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#create-your-own","content":"Implement `generate` with the exact keyword-only signature, carry `name` +\n`Config` (`extra=\"forbid\"`), and decorate with `@register_inference(\"<name>\")`:"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#create-your-own","content":"Then reference it by `kind`:"},"1157":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Expose it as an entry point under the group `evsys_sdk.inference` in your\npackage's `pyproject.toml`:"},"1158":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-34","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"On import `evsys_sdk` walks that group and runs your `@register_inference`\ndecorator, so the `kind` is available from any project with no fork."},"1159":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-35","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Data stores\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores\" />"},"1160":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-36","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Callbacks\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks\" />"},"1161":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference-37","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/inference#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1162":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","type":"page","content":"Log stores","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores"},"1163":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","content":"Where metrics, hyperparameters, and artifact pointers go as training proceeds."},"1164":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1165":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1166":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1167":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1168":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","content":"A **log store** is the sink the training loop writes to as it runs: scalar\nmetrics per step, the run's hyperparameters, and pointers to artifacts\n(checkpoints, files). The default writes JSONL under the run directory. You make\nyour own when you want metrics to flow somewhere specific (TensorBoard, a\ndatabase, several places at once)."},"1169":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"The contract is `evsys_sdk.protocols.LogStore` (a `typing.Protocol`). An\nimplementation declares `name` and five methods:"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key / YAML `kind`."},"1171":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`log_scalar(self, key: str, value: float, step: int) -> None`** — record a\nsingle named scalar `value` at training `step`. The one-metric convenience\nform of `log_metrics`."},"1172":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`log_metrics(self, metrics: dict[str, float], step: int, *, split: str = \"train\") -> None`**\n— record a whole dict of named metrics at `step`. The `split` argument is\n**keyword-only** (note the `*,`) and defaults to `\"train\"`. It tags which\nside of the train/val firewall the row belongs to: pass `split=\"val\"` for\nin-loop validation metrics so train and validation curves stay distinguishable\nin the same log. (The JSONL store writes `split` as a field on each row; the\nTensorBoard store ignores it because the split is already baked into the\nmetric keys like `val/loss`.)"},"1173":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`log_hyperparams(self, params: dict[str, Any]) -> None`** — record the run's\nhyperparameters once. Values can be any JSON-serializable type, not just\nfloats. The JSONL store merges repeated calls into one file."},"1174":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`log_artifact(self, name: str, path: str, *, kind: str = \"file\") -> None`**\n— register a produced artifact under a logical `name` pointing at `path`. The\n`kind` argument is **keyword-only** and defaults to `\"file\"` (use it to mark\ne.g. `\"checkpoint\"`). Stores the pointer, not the bytes."},"1175":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#the-contract","content":"**`close(self) -> None`** — flush and release resources at run end. After\nclose, the JSONL store refuses further writes."},"1176":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1177":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does / where it writes"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`jsonl`"},"1179":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`JSONLLogStore` (`src/evsys_sdk/log_stores/jsonl.py`). Append-only. Under `log_dir&#x60; it writes three files: &#x2A;*`metrics.jsonl`** (one JSON object per `log_scalar`/`log_metrics` call, each row `{ts, step, split, metrics}&#x60;), &#x2A;*`hyperparams.json`** (the merged hyperparameter dict, re-read and updated on each `log_hyperparams&#x60;), and &#x2A;*`artifacts.json`** (a growing list of `{name, path, kind, ts}` from `log_artifact`). File names are configurable via `metrics_file` / `hyperparams_file` / `artifacts_file`. In a standard run the dir is `<run_dir>/logs/`."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`tensorboard`"},"1181":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`TensorBoardLogStore` (`src/evsys_sdk/log_stores/tensorboard.py`). Wraps a `torch.utils.tensorboard.SummaryWriter` (optional dependency — the module raises `ImportError` at load if torch/tensorboard is missing). Metrics become `add_scalar` events; hyperparameters and artifacts become `add_text`. `log_metrics`' `split` is ignored (it's already in the keys). Constructor params: `log_dir`, `flush_secs` (default 30)."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`multiplex`"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"`MultiplexLogStore` (`src/evsys_sdk/log_stores/multiplex.py`). Fans every call out to a list of child stores. Param `children` is a list of `{kind, params}` specs it instantiates on construction (each looked up via the log-store registry). `close()` is best-effort per child (errors swallowed). Use it to write JSONL **and** TensorBoard from one run."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#use-a-built-in","content":"A multiplex config:"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#create-your-own","content":"Implement the five methods, carry `name` + a `Config` model (`extra=\"forbid\"`),\nand decorate with `@register_log_store(\"<name>\")`:"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#create-your-own","content":"Then in YAML:"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Expose it as an entry point under the group `evsys_sdk.log_stores` in your\npackage's `pyproject.toml`:"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"On import `evsys_sdk` walks that group and runs your `@register_log_store`\ndecorator, so the `kind` is usable from any project with no fork."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Data stores\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/data-stores\" />"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Callbacks\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/callbacks\" />"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/log-stores#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","type":"page","content":"Metrics","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","content":"Reducers that collapse per-task, per-sample rewards into one benchmark scalar."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","content":"A **metric** reduces a benchmark's raw rewards to a single number. A benchmark\nscores each task by running its verifier on `num_samples` rollouts, producing a\nlist of per-sample rewards per task; a metric takes that whole `list[list[float]]`\nand returns one float (`pass_rate`, `pass@3`, …). You list metrics by name on a\nbenchmark and write your own when you need a reduction the built-ins don't cover."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#the-contract","content":"Defined in `src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py` as `class Metric(Protocol)`. A metric is\nsimpler than the other plugins — it has &#x2A;*no `Config`** (metrics take no params):"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key; the string you put on a benchmark's\n`metrics:` list."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#the-contract","content":"**`def compute(self, task_rewards: Sequence[Sequence[float]]) -> float`** — the\none method. `task_rewards` is a sequence of sequences: **one inner sequence per\ntask**, holding that task's per-sample rewards. (So `task_rewards[i][j]` is the\nreward of sample `j` on task `i`.) It returns a single `float` — the aggregated\nscore for the benchmark. A sample is treated as \"passing\" when its reward\nclears `PASS_THRESHOLD` (`1.0`, defined in `metrics/basic.py`)."},"1202":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`mean_reward`"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"**Macro** mean reward: for each task take the mean of its samples, then average those task-means. Empty tasks are skipped; returns `0.0` if there are none."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`avg`"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"Alias of `mean_reward` (same `compute`, different name)."},"1208":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`pass_rate`"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"**Micro** pass rate: total passing samples ÷ total samples, pooled across all tasks (`0.0` if no samples)."},"1210":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`pass@1`"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"Fraction of tasks where **any** of the first **1** sample passes."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`pass@3`"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"Fraction of tasks where **any** of the first **3** samples passes (`any(_passes(r) for r in rs[:3])`)."},"1214":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"`pass^3`"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"\"pass-hat-3\" / consistency: fraction of tasks where **all** of the first **3** samples pass."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#use-a-built-in","content":"> **Economics metrics come free, separately.** Per-task **time, tokens, and\n> cost** are *not* part of this metric registry. They are harbor-native: they\n> come from each rollout's usage (surfaced via `Trajectory.metadata['usage']`\n> and aggregated into eval metrics), so you get them automatically without\n> registering or listing anything. The metric registry here is only for reducing\n> *rewards* to a scalar."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Register a metric from a separate pip package via the entry-point group\n`evsys_sdk.metrics` in its `pyproject.toml`:"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"`evsys_sdk` walks that group on import and runs the `@register_metric` decorator."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"🔧 Transforms\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms\" />"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"✅ Verifiers\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers\" />"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"🧩 Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","type":"page","content":"Transforms","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","content":"Ordered row-rewriters that turn raw dataset rows into the standardized rows your algorithm consumes."},"1224":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","content":"A **transform** is a small, named function-object that rewrites the rows of a\ndataset. Raw data on disk (`{query, answer, ...}`) almost never matches the\nshape an algorithm wants (`{messages: [...]}`); transforms bridge that gap. You\nlist them on a dataset, they run **in order**, and each one takes the rows the\nprevious one emitted. Write your own when your raw data has a layout no built-in\nknows how to read."},"1229":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"The protocol lives in `src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py` as `class Transform(Protocol)`.\nA transform is any object that declares two class vars and is *callable*:"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key. This is the exact string you put\nas `kind:` in YAML."},"1231":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model (with `extra=\"forbid\"`)\ndescribing the transform's params. The factory validates the `params:` block\nfrom YAML against this model before constructing the transform, so an unknown\nor mistyped param fails loudly instead of being silently ignored."},"1232":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"**`def __call__(self, rows: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]) -> Iterable[dict[str, Any]]`**\n— the one method. It receives `rows`, an iterable of plain dicts (one dict per\ndata row, exactly as read from the JSONL/parquet source or as emitted by the\nprevious transform), and returns an iterable of dicts. There is no fixed schema\non the dicts — keys are whatever your data has. The convention is **additive**:\nkeep the original keys and add new ones (`yield {**row, \"messages\": ...}`) so a\nlater transform or the algorithm can still see the source fields. Returning a\ngenerator is fine and encouraged — rows stream through lazily."},"1233":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#the-contract","content":"Because transforms are chained, the *output row shape of one transform is the\ninput row shape of the next*. The last transform in the list must emit rows in\nwhatever standardized shape the algorithm expects (e.g. SFT wants a `messages`\nlist; an RL data path wants `HarborTask`-shaped rows)."},"1234":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"`jsonl_to_chat`"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"Turns each raw row into `{..., \"messages\": [...]}`. Adds a `system` message if `system_prompt` is set, a `user` message from `user_template.format(**row)`, and — if `assistant_template` is given (SFT) — an `assistant` message from `assistant_template.format(**row)`. Templates are Python format strings whose `{field}` placeholders pull from the row's keys."},"1238":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"`identity`"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#use-a-built-in","content":"Pass-through: returns the rows unchanged (`iter(rows)`). Useful for tests or when raw data is already in the right shape. Its `Config` has no fields."},"1240":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#create-your-own","content":"Then reference it by its registered name in YAML:"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"To register a transform from a separate pip package (no SDK edit, no import in\nyour project), declare a Python **entry point** under the group\n`evsys_sdk.transforms` in that package's `pyproject.toml`:"},"1242":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"On import, `evsys_sdk` walks that group and loads each target, running its\n`@register_transform` decorator."},"1243":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"✅ Verifiers\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers\" />"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"📊 Metrics\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics\" />"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"🧩 Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"page","content":"Verifiers","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Concepts","Concepts","Plugins"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers"},"1247":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-0","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","content":"Two reward mechanisms — the Verifier class registry and the in-process verifier-fn registry referenced from task data."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-1","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#a-the-verifier-class-registry","content":"(a) The Verifier class registry"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-2","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"1250":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-3","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in","content":"Use a built-in"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-4","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#create-your-own","content":"Create your own"},"1252":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-5","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"(b) The in-process verifier-fn registry"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-6","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"Use a built-in fn"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#create-your-own-fn","content":"Create your own fn"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"Ship it in a package"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","content":"A **verifier** turns a model's completion into a reward. The SDK has **two\ndistinct verifier mechanisms** that are easy to confuse, so read this first:"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","content":"**The `Verifier` class registry** — full plugin classes (`name` + `Config` +\n`verify(...)`), registered with `@register_verifier` and selected by `kind:`.\nThis is the general extension point."},"1258":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","content":"**The in-process verifier-fn registry** — plain Python *functions* that live\ninside the SDK and are referenced **by name from task data**. A `HarborTask`\ncarries `verifier: {kind: in_process, fn_name: ...}`, and `fn_name` resolves\nto one of these functions. The remote backend never stores verifier *code* —\nonly the `fn_name` plus per-task `expected`/`params`."},"1259":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","content":"Both produce a reward; the difference is *who owns the spec* (a config author vs.\neach individual task row) and *the shape of the callable*."},"1260":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"Defined in `src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py` as `class Verifier(Protocol)`, alongside\nthe result dataclass:"},"1261":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"A verifier class declares two class vars and one method:"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key / YAML `kind`."},"1263":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — Pydantic model (`extra=\"forbid\"`) for the\nverifier's params; `params:` from YAML is validated against it."},"1264":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#the-contract","content":"**`def verify(self, *, prompt: str, completion: str, target: dict[str, Any]) -> VerificationResult`**\n— all three arguments are **keyword-only**. `prompt` is the input text the\nmodel saw; `completion` is the model's generated text; `target` is a dict of\ngold/reference data for this example (answer keys, expected fields, etc.). It\nreturns a `VerificationResult` whose `reward` is a float and whose `info` is a\nfree-form dict of diagnostics (surfaced for debugging, not used for training)."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in","content":"Built-in"},"1266":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in","content":"What it does"},"1267":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in","content":"`format_only`"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in","content":"Rewards **structure only**, ignoring correctness. `verify` checks whether `completion` contains both `<think>`/`</think>` (adds `has_think_reward`, default `0.5`) and `<answer>`/`</answer>` (adds `has_answer_reward`, default `0.5`). Returns the summed reward and `info={\"has_think\": ..., \"has_answer\": ...}`. Handy as a warm-up reward so a model first learns the output format."},"1269":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"These are **functions**, not classes, and they live in\n`src/evsys_sdk/verifiers/fns.py`. They are the single source of truth for cheap\nPython verification logic. A task references one by name:"},"1270":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"At score time the runner looks up `fn_name` via `fns.get(fn_name)` and calls the\nfunction. Every verifier-fn shares this exact signature:"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"**`model_output: str`** — the model's completion text."},"1272":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"**`expected: Any`** — the gold value from the task's `expected` field (string,\ndict, etc., depending on the fn)."},"1273":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"**`params: dict`** — the task's `params` block, a plain dict of options."},"1274":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#b-the-in-process-verifier-fn-registry","content":"**returns `float`** — the reward, typically `1.0` (pass) or `0.0` (fail)."},"1275":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`fn_name`"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"Exact signature & behavior"},"1277":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`exact_match`"},"1278":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`exact_match(model_output, expected, params) -> float`. Strips whitespace from both sides; if `params[\"ignore_case\"]` is truthy, lower-cases both; returns `1.0` on exact string equality else `0.0`."},"1279":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`contains`"},"1280":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`contains(model_output, expected, params) -> float`. Returns `1.0` if `str(expected)` is a non-empty substring of `model_output` (case-folded when `params[\"ignore_case\"]`), else `0.0`."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-34","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`regex_match`"},"1282":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-35","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`regex_match(model_output, expected, params) -> float`. Treats `expected` as a regex; returns `1.0` if `re.search` finds it in `model_output` (with `re.IGNORECASE` when `params[\"ignore_case\"]`), else `0.0`."},"1283":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-36","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`tool_calls_match`"},"1284":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-37","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#use-a-built-in-fn","content":"`tool_calls_match(model_output, expected, params) -> float`. Parses both `model_output` and `expected` as JSON dicts (stripping code fences). Returns `1.0` only if `tool` and `action` match; any `ref`/`text` present in `expected` must match; and a `coordinate` must be within `params[\"coordinate_tolerance\"]` (default `25`) on both axes. Otherwise `0.0`."},"1285":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-38","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#create-your-own-fn","content":"Register a function with the `@register_fn` decorator (or `register(name, fn)`)\nfrom `evsys_sdk.verifiers.fns`:"},"1286":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-39","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#create-your-own-fn","content":"Then a task can reference it: `verifier: {kind: in_process, fn_name: startswith, expected: \"Answer:\", params: {ignore_case: true}}`."},"1287":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-40","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#create-your-own-fn","content":"> **Which one do I use?** Use a **verifier-fn** for sub-millisecond per-task\n> checks where each task carries its own `expected` (tool-call matching,\n> exact-match, boxed answers). Use a **Verifier class** when the reward logic is\n> config-level and shared across tasks, or needs richer params via `Config`."},"1288":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-41","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"A `Verifier` **class** can be registered from an external package via the\nentry-point group `evsys_sdk.verifiers` in its `pyproject.toml`:"},"1289":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-42","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"(Verifier *fns* are registered in-process with `@register_fn` at import time;\nthey are not loaded through entry points.)"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-43","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"🔧 Transforms\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/transforms\" />"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-44","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"📊 Metrics\" href=\"/docs/concepts/plugins/metrics\" />"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers-45","page_id":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/plugins/verifiers#ship-it-in-a-package","content":"<Card title=\"🧩 Extensibility\" href=\"/docs/concepts/extensibility\" />"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","type":"page","content":"_entry_points","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","_entry_points"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points"},"1294":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","content":"Load third-party extensions registered via Python entry points."},"1295":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","content":"External packages declare extensions in their pyproject.toml:"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","content":"\\[project.entry-points.\"evsys\\_sdk.algorithms\"]\nmy\\_dpo = \"my\\_pkg.algorithms:MyDPO\""},"1297":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","content":"When evsys\\_sdk imports, we walk those groups and import each\ntarget module — its top-level @register\\_\\* decorators run, populating our\nregistries. No fork required."},"1298":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_entry_points","content":"Failures here are non-fatal: a third-party package with an import error\nshouldn't break the library. We log a warning and continue."},"1299":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","type":"page","content":"HarborUploadResult","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","_harbor_upload"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult"},"1300":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1301":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult#functions","content":"Functions"},"1302":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","content":"Result of one harbor upload call."},"1303":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult#attributes","content":"`\"created\" | \"updated\" | \"unchanged\"`."},"1304":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","type":"page","content":"_harbor_upload","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","_harbor_upload"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload"},"1305":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Shared upload logic for harbor-format directories."},"1306":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"`benchmark_upload` registers a local `\\<dir>/` (`tasks.jsonl` +\n`metadata.yaml`) with the dashboard. The reusable body lives here and the\nwrapper passes in its create/add-rows/list callables, so a future harbor-style\nentity can reuse it."},"1307":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Re-uploading the same content is a no-op (we hash `tasks.jsonl`);\nre-uploading changed content registers a new version."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;HarborUploadResult&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload/HarborUploadResult&#x22;\" />"},"1309":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Upload (or re-upload) a harbor directory via the supplied store callables."},"1310":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Steps:"},"1311":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Load with `Benchmark.from_dir` (catches malformed jsonl / metadata)."},"1312":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Hash `tasks.jsonl` content for idempotency."},"1313":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Look up an existing record with the same `name`:"},"1314":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"same hash → return `\"unchanged\"`."},"1315":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"different hash → create a new version row, push tasks."},"1316":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-11","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"none → create version 1, push tasks."},"1317":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload-12","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/_harbor_upload","content":"Return the highest-version record with `name`, if any."},"1318":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","type":"page","content":"backends","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","backends"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","content":"Built-in backends. Importing this module registers them."},"1320":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/backends/local&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;local&#x22;\" />"},"1321":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/backends/tinker&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;tinker&#x22;\" />"},"1322":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/backends","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/backends/mock&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;mock&#x22;\" />"},"1323":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","type":"page","content":"algorithms","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","algorithms"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms"},"1324":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"Built-in algorithms."},"1325":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"Each algorithm targets a specific (recipe-kind, backend-kind) pair via the\nregistry: the algorithm's `name` is what users put in `algorithm.kind:` of\nthe YAML; routing to a specific backend happens inside the algorithm's\n.train() (it inspects ctx.backend.name)."},"1326":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"Some algorithms are backend-agnostic (Mock); most route to a single backend."},"1327":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/mock_rl&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;mock_rl&#x22;\" />"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/sdft&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;sdft&#x22;\" />"},"1329":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/rl&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;rl&#x22;\" />"},"1330":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/sft&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;sft&#x22;\" />"},"1331":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/combo&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;combo&#x22;\" />"},"1332":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/local_rl&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;local_rl&#x22;\" />"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/local_sft&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;local_sft&#x22;\" />"},"1334":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/gepa_prompt&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;gepa_prompt&#x22;\" />"},"1335":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-11","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/base&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;base&#x22;\" />"},"1336":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms-12","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/algorithms/mock_sft&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;mock_sft&#x22;\" />"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","type":"page","content":"Benchmark","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark"},"1338":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1339":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Functions"},"1340":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","content":"A harbor-format eval suite loaded into memory."},"1341":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","content":"Two builders:"},"1342":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","content":"`from_dir(path)`   — `data/benchmark/\\<name>/\\{tasks.jsonl,metadata.yaml\\}`"},"1343":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","content":"`from_iterable(name, rows, metadata=...)` — for tests / programmatic."},"1344":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","content":"`score(client)` runs inference + verification and returns a `BenchmarkScore`."},"1345":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#attributes","content":"Filesystem dir the benchmark was loaded from (None if in-memory)."},"1346":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Resolve a benchmark spec `\\{path | id | name\\}` to a `Benchmark`."},"1347":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"The single resolver shared by the experiment config, the standalone\n`run_benchmark`, and the CLI — so all accept the same references:"},"1348":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`path` → local harbor dir (delegates to `from_dir`); offline / dev."},"1349":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-11","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`id`   → dashboard benchmark id, pulled into the local `.evsys/`."},"1350":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-12","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`name` → resolved to the latest version's id, then pulled."},"1351":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-13","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Returns `None` when the spec carries none of those. `store` is\nneeded only for the id / name paths."},"1352":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-14","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Run each task through `client` and score the completion."},"1353":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-15","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Sequential — wrap in a thread/process pool externally if you need\nconcurrency. (Most local clients are GPU-bound and don't benefit.)"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-16","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`prompt_builder(task) -> str` lets callers shape the model input;\ndefault is `task.instruction` verbatim."},"1355":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-17","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`breakdown_keys` are dotted attribute paths into `task.metadata`. Each\nkey produces `\\{value -> \\{n, mean_reward, pass_rate\\}\\}` in the result."},"1356":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-18","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"`limit` caps how many tasks are scored — the first `limit` in\n`self.tasks` (deterministic, in benchmark order). Useful for fast\nsmoke-runs on large benchmarks. `None` means score everything."},"1357":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-19","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Score this benchmark through harbor's rollout engine — the harbor\ncounterpart of :meth:`score`, returning the same :class:`BenchmarkScore`."},"1358":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark-20","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark#functions","content":"Each task is rolled out `num_samples` times (one verifier reward per\nsample); `metrics` (registry names like `pass@3`) reduce the per-task\nsample rewards, and `time/tokens/cost_per_task` come from harbor usage.\n`model_client` is `\"tinker\"` (on-policy checkpoint, needs\n`model_path`) or `\"litellm\"` (closed/API model; `model_name` a\nlitellm string). The result's :attr:`BenchmarkScore.rollouts` carries the\nraw per-(task, sample) rollouts so callers can upload eval predictions\nwithout re-running."},"1359":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","type":"page","content":"BenchmarkScore","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore"},"1360":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1361":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#functions","content":"Functions"},"1362":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","content":"Aggregate output of `Benchmark.score`."},"1363":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"Top-level aggregates: `mean_reward`, `pass_rate`, `n_tasks`."},"1364":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"One entry per task in the same order as `Benchmark.tasks`."},"1365":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"`\\{bucket_field: \\{bucket_value: \\{n, mean_reward, pass_rate\\}\\}\\}`."},"1366":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"Populated when `score(..., breakdown_keys=[...])` is passed. Each bucket\nfield is an attribute path into a task's `metadata` (e.g. `\"toolkit\"`)."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore#attributes","content":"Raw per-(task, sample) harbor rollouts (token ids + reward + usage), in\ntask order; populated by `score_via_harbor`, empty for in-process `score()`.\nLets callers upload per-sample eval predictions without re-running."},"1368":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","type":"page","content":"BenchmarkTaskResult","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult"},"1369":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult#functions","content":"Functions"},"1371":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult","content":"One scored task."},"1372":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","type":"page","content":"benchmark","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"Benchmark — load a harbor-format eval suite and score a model against it."},"1374":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"A benchmark on disk is a directory:"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"data/benchmark/\\<name>/\ntasks.jsonl       # required — one HarborTask per line\nmetadata.yaml     # optional — description, version, source, splits, ...\nimages/           # optional — referenced by relative path from tasks\nraw/              # optional — pre-harbor source for traceability"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"`Benchmark.from_dir(path)` loads the suite. `bench.score(client)` runs each\ntask's `instruction` through an `InferenceClient`, then scores the completion\nvia the SDK's in-process verifier-fn registry (`verifiers/fns.py`). The result\ncollects per-task rows, top-level aggregates (`mean_reward`, `pass_rate`,\n`n_tasks`), and optional breakdown buckets (e.g. per-toolkit pass rate) keyed\nby an attribute path into `metadata`."},"1377":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"E2B and LLM-judge verifiers are recognized but not executed here — they need\nnetwork / sandboxes and live behind their own runners. Tasks carrying those\nverifier kinds raise a clear error so callers don't silently mis-score."},"1378":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;BenchmarkTaskResult&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkTaskResult&#x22;\" />"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;BenchmarkScore&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/BenchmarkScore&#x22;\" />"},"1380":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;Benchmark&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark/Benchmark&#x22;\" />"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark","content":"Bucket per-task rewards by each dotted `metadata` key →\n`\\{key: \\{value: \\{n, mean_reward, pass_rate\\}\\}\\}`. Shared by the in-process\nand harbor scoring paths."},"1382":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","type":"page","content":"benchmark_run","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark_run"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run#by-local-path-dashboard-id-or-name--same-resolver-as-the-config","content":"by local path, dashboard id, or name — same resolver as the config"},"1384":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","content":"Standalone benchmark run — score a benchmark on a model, no training."},"1385":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","content":"Reuses the *same* harbor rollout path as in-training eval\n(:func:`evsys_sdk.training.harbor_eval.score_via_harbor`) plus the same metrics\nand eval-rollout upload. The only differences from a post-training eval: there's\nno checkpoint, and the rollout LLM is a closed / API model via litellm\n(`model_client=\"litellm\"`). Rollouts persist under the local `.evsys/`\nworkspace and, when a `store` + `run_id` are given, push to the dashboard."},"1386":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","content":"from evsys\\_sdk import run\\_benchmark"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run#by-local-path-dashboard-id-or-name--same-resolver-as-the-config","content":"metrics = run\\_benchmark(path=\"data/benchmark/tool-search\",\nmodel=\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-1\")\nmetrics = run\\_benchmark(id=\"bench\\_abc123\", model=\"openai/gpt-4o\", store=store)"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run#by-local-path-dashboard-id-or-name--same-resolver-as-the-config","content":"API keys come from the standard provider env vars (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, …)."},"1389":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run#by-local-path-dashboard-id-or-name--same-resolver-as-the-config","content":"Score a benchmark on a closed / API `model` through harbor — no training."},"1390":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_run#by-local-path-dashboard-id-or-name--same-resolver-as-the-config","content":"The benchmark is given directly (`benchmark=`) or resolved by\n`path` / `id` / `name` via the shared :meth:`Benchmark.load` resolver\n(same references the config accepts). `model` is a litellm string, e.g.\n`\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-1\"` / `\"openai/gpt-4o\"`; repeats use the\nper-task `num_samples` in one async harbor job. Returns the eval metric\ndict (mean\\_reward, pass\\_rate, n\\_tasks, and time/tokens/cost per task), and\nuploads the per-task eval rollouts when both `store` and `run_id` are set."},"1391":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","type":"page","content":"UploadResult","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark_upload"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult"},"1392":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1393":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult#functions","content":"Functions"},"1394":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","content":"Result of one upload call."},"1395":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult#attributes","content":"`\"created\" | \"updated\" | \"unchanged\"`."},"1396":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","type":"page","content":"benchmark_upload","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","benchmark_upload"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"Register a local harbor-format benchmark with the dashboard."},"1398":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"Each `data/benchmark/\\<name>/` directory becomes a row in the dashboard's\nbenchmark table so experiments can reference it by id. Re-uploading the\nsame content is a no-op (we hash `tasks.jsonl`); re-uploading changed\ncontent registers a new version."},"1399":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"CLI entry point: `evsys benchmark upload data/benchmark/\\<name>`.\nProgrammatic: `upload_benchmark(store, path)`."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"The harbor upload body lives in `_harbor_upload.upload_harbor` (reusable for\nother harbor-format entities) — this module only wires the benchmark store\nmethods and keeps the historical `UploadResult` shape."},"1401":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;UploadResult&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload/UploadResult&#x22;\" />"},"1402":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"Upload (or re-upload) a harbor benchmark directory."},"1403":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/benchmark_upload","content":"See `_harbor_upload.upload_harbor` for the shared idempotency logic."},"1404":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","type":"page","content":"Checkpoint","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","checkpoint"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#functions","content":"Functions"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","content":"One row of a `checkpoints.jsonl` manifest."},"1408":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"The `name` field — e.g. `\"final\"`, `\"epoch-3\"`, or a step string."},"1409":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"Training step / batch index, if recorded (`batch` in tinker)."},"1410":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"Training-state checkpoint URI (`state_path` in tinker)."},"1411":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"Inference-ready sampler URI; what you pass to a sampling client."},"1412":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#attributes","content":"Untouched manifest row, for fields not modeled above."},"1413":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#functions","content":"Pick the one to evaluate against."},"1414":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint#functions","content":"Strategy: prefer an explicit `name == \"final\"` row that exposes a\npath, else the last row that exposes a path, else None."},"1415":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","type":"page","content":"checkpoint","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","checkpoint"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint"},"1416":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Checkpoint — parse the `checkpoints.jsonl` manifests algorithms write."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Tinker SFT/RL (and any other algorithm that follows the same convention)\nappends one JSON row per saved checkpoint to `\\<output_dir>/checkpoints.jsonl`:"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"\\{\"name\": \"final\", \"batch\": 1520, \"epoch\": 10,\n\"state\\_path\": \"tinker://...\", \"sampler\\_path\": \"tinker://...\"}"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Researcher scripts repeatedly hand-roll a few lines to find this manifest,\nparse it, and pick the right row to evaluate against. This module gives them:"},"1420":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"`Checkpoint` — one row, typed."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"`read_manifest(path)` — full ordered list."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"`find_manifest(run_dir)` — locate the manifest under a run directory."},"1423":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"`Checkpoint.pick_final(checkpoints)` — pick the \"evaluate me\" row\n(prefer `name == \"final\"`, else the last row that exposes a path)."},"1424":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;Checkpoint&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint/Checkpoint&#x22;\" />"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Parse a checkpoints.jsonl into ordered Checkpoint rows."},"1426":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Blank lines are skipped; malformed JSON raises `ValueError` (don't\nsilently lose checkpoint pointers — the eval step depends on them)."},"1427":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-11","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Locate `checkpoints.jsonl` under `run_dir` (recursive)."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint-12","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/checkpoint","content":"Algorithms sometimes nest the manifest under a sub-directory\n(e.g. `\\<run_dir>/\\<sub>/checkpoints.jsonl`); search shallowest-first\nand return the first match. Returns `None` if no manifest exists."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","type":"page","content":"constants","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","constants"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","content":"Central constants for the evsys\\_sdk SDK."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","content":"Single source of truth for env-var names, defaults, HTTP endpoint paths,\nstatus strings, and logging config. Change endpoints / defaults here — not\nscattered across the codebase."},"1432":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","content":"Distinct from `config.py`, which holds the user-facing Pydantic *experiment*\nconfig models (ExperimentConfig, RunConfig, ...). This module is SDK app-level\nplumbing."},"1433":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/constants","content":"Interpret an env var string as a boolean."},"1434":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","type":"page","content":"cli","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","cli"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","content":"evsys CLI."},"1436":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/cli","content":"Score a benchmark (by --path / --id / --name) on a closed/API model."},"1437":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","type":"page","content":"DashboardClient","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","dashboard_client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Functions"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","content":"HTTP client for the EvolvingSystems backend's SDK write routes, with a local\nmirror and graceful degradation when the backend is unreachable."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"POST to the backend. Returns the JSON dict, or None when the write\ncould not be sent remotely (offline, or backend unreachable). Raises\nDashboardClientError on a 4xx response."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"PATCH experiment metadata. Whitelisted backend fields: status,\nbest\\_score, best\\_generation\\_id, current\\_iteration, error\\_message,\nhypothesis, hypothesis\\_reasoning, plan, conclusion, tags,\nproblem\\_statement\\_id, is\\_valid."},"1443":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"e.g. `update_experiment(exp_id, is_valid=False)` to invalidate an\nexperiment after a bug is found in its runs (D16)."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Log per-step training metrics as long-format run\\_metrics (D15)."},"1445":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Accepts arbitrary named series via `**metrics` (e.g. `val_loss=…`,\n`kl_loss=…`) plus a `split` (`train`/`val`/`test`). The named\nkwargs (loss, accuracy, …) are folded into the same `metrics` map.\nNone values are dropped."},"1446":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Record an eval (D13): a run scored on a benchmark → metrics\\{name:value}."},"1447":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Record a named checkpoint for a run (D7)."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient#functions","content":"Bulk-insert per-task predictions. Each is:\n\\{ kind: 'eval' | 'rollout', eval\\_id?, task\\_id?, sample\\_idx?, step?,\ninstruction, model\\_output, expected?, reward?, advantage?, metadata? }"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","type":"page","content":"DashboardClientError","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","dashboard_client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError#functions","content":"Functions"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError","content":"Raised on a 4xx response (auth / membership / bad request)."},"1453":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError","type":"page","content":"EvsysAuthError","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","dashboard_client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError","content":"Raised when credentials are missing and offline mode is not enabled."},"1455":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","type":"page","content":"ExperimentRun","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","dashboard_client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun#functions","content":"Functions"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","content":"One generation in one experiment, lifecycle-managed."},"1459":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","content":"Use as a context manager. On clean exit, the generation + experiment are\nmarked completed (with the best score / generation\\_id). On raised\nexception, both are marked failed with the exception message. All writes\nare mirrored locally and degrade gracefully if the backend is down."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun#functions","content":"One- or two-line takeaway from the run. Flushed on clean **exit**."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","type":"page","content":"dashboard_client","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","dashboard_client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"DashboardClient — push SDK runs to the EvolvingSystems backend, with a local mirror."},"1463":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Architecture: SDK → Django HTTP → Supabase. The user holds an API key (the\nsame key the dashboard issues at `Settings → API keys`) plus a project id\n(shared by everyone on the project, set in the SDK env). The SDK calls\n`/api/dashboard/api/sdk/...` routes; the backend authenticates the key, checks\nthe user belongs to the project, and writes Supabase with its service key."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Robustness (wandb-offline style):"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Every write is **also** mirrored to a local folder (`EVSYS_LOG_DIR`,\ndefault `./evsys_sdk`). There is no remote-only mode."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"If the backend is unreachable (connection error / timeout / 5xx) the call\nlogs a warning and keeps going with the local mirror — it does not crash."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-5","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Auth is required by default: without an API key + project id the client\nraises. Set `EVSYS_OFFLINE=true` (or `offline=True`) to run with no\nauth, writing only to the local mirror."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-6","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Env vars (see constants.py): EVSYS\\_API\\_URL, EVSYS\\_API\\_KEY,\nEVSYS\\_PROJECT\\_ID, EVSYS\\_LOG\\_DIR, EVSYS\\_OFFLINE,\nEVSYS\\_LOGGING\\_LEVEL."},"1469":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-7","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"Quick usage::"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-8","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"from evsys\\_sdk import DashboardClient, ExperimentRun"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-9","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"client = DashboardClient()  # reads env vars"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-10","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"with ExperimentRun(client, experiment\\_name=\"sft\\_run\\_v9\",\nrecipe\\_kind=\"sft\",\nrun\\_config=\\{\"lr\": 1e-5, \"batch\\_size\": 16}) as run:\nfor step in range(1, 1001):\nrun.log\\_step(step, loss=...)\nrun.log\\_eval(metrics=\\{\"pass\\_at\\_1\": 0.83}, benchmark\\_id=\"...\")\nrun.set\\_best\\_score(0.83)"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-11","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;DashboardClientError&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClientError&#x22;\" />"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-12","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;EvsysAuthError&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/EvsysAuthError&#x22;\" />"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-13","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;DashboardClient&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/DashboardClient&#x22;\" />"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client-14","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client","content":"<Card title=\"&#x22;ExperimentRun&#x22;\" href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/dashboard_client/ExperimentRun&#x22;\" />"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","type":"page","content":"data_stores","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_stores"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","content":"Built-in data stores. Importing this module registers them."},"1479":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores/local&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;local&#x22;\" />"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores","content":"<Card href=\"&#x22;/docs/evsys_sdk/data_stores/in_memory&#x22;\" title=\"&#x22;in_memory&#x22;\" />"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","type":"page","content":"ChatMessagesRow","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow#functions","content":"Functions"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","content":"One SFT conversation — pure data, no supervision encoded."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","content":"`messages` is the full multi-turn conversation (roles: system / user /\nassistant / tool). The row deliberately carries **no** notion of which\ntokens are trained: choosing the supervised span is the *algorithm's* job\n(e.g. `SFT` masks assistant turns according to its `supervise`\nconfig). Keeping the dataset format free of target/loss metadata lets the\nsame conversation feed any SFT variant."},"1486":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/ChatMessagesRow","content":"For multimodal SFT, a message's `content` may be either a string OR a\nlist of content blocks (mix of text + image blocks). See\n`image_url_block` / `image_base64_block` helpers below."},"1487":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","type":"page","content":"E2BVerifier","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier#functions","content":"Functions"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","content":"Sandboxed code verifier — runs `test_state.py` inside an E2B container."},"1491":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/E2BVerifier","content":"The runner builds the container per the `dockerfile`, drops in the\nmodel's completion + `test_state.py`, executes `test_sh` (default\n`pytest -q test_state.py`), and reads pass/fail from the exit code."},"1492":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","type":"page","content":"HarborTask","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask#functions","content":"Functions"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","content":"One RL task — instruction + verifier spec."},"1496":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/HarborTask","content":"Same shape whether the task came from a hand-written eval set, an HF\ndataset, or a generated rollout corpus. Runners materialize the prompt by\nfeeding `instruction` to the policy, generate a rollout, and score it\nusing `verifier` (whichever variant — see `VerifierPayload`)."},"1497":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","type":"page","content":"InProcessVerifier","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier"},"1498":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier#functions","content":"Functions"},"1500":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","content":"Cheap Python-function verifier."},"1501":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/InProcessVerifier","content":"The runner looks up `fn_name` in a registered verifier-fn map and calls\nit with `(completion, expected, **params)`. Sub-millisecond — use this\nfor tool-call matching, exact-match, boxed-answer parsing."},"1502":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","type":"page","content":"LLMJudgeVerifier","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier#functions","content":"Functions"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","content":"LLM judge — `judge_model` scores the completion against `rubric`."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/LLMJudgeVerifier","content":"The runner calls the judge model with the rubric + completion and parses a\nnumeric score from the response (usually in a `\\boxed\\{\\}` or\n`\\<score>...\\</score>` tag)."},"1507":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","type":"page","content":"PromptExample","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample#functions","content":"Functions"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","content":"One example for prompt-search / GEPA-style optimization."},"1511":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/PromptExample","content":"`inputs` is a dict of named task inputs; `expected` is the gold output\nthe score function compares the model's completion against."},"1512":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat","type":"page","content":"TargetFormat","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types/TargetFormat#attributes","content":"Attributes"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","type":"page","content":"data_types","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Api","evsys_sdk","data_types"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types"},"1515":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types-0","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","content":"Harbor-compatible data shapes."},"1516":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types-1","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","content":"The schemas runners consume and dashboards render. Mirrors the production\ninternal types so JSONL files round-trip between this SDK and the internal\nserving / dashboard stack without conversion."},"1517":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types-2","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","content":"Two row formats:"},"1518":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types-3","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","content":"`ChatMessagesRow`  — SFT example  (messages prefix + supervised target)"},"1519":{"id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types-4","page_id":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/evsys_sdk/data_types","content":"`HarborTask`       — RL task      (i