ry `on_step_end`\n(split `\"train\"`) and `on_eval` (split `\"val\"`). Each row is\n`{step, split, metrics}`."],[1085,"**`<output_dir>/<run_key>/predictions/<name>.jsonl`** — written per benchmark in\n`on_benchmark_eval` when predictions are present (`<name>` is the eval name,\nslashes/spaces sanitized), one prediction row per line."],[1086,"**`<output_dir>/<run_key>/summary.md`** — written at `on_run_end`: the run key,\nthe hypothesis (echoed in the header), final status, and one line per benchmark\neval with its metrics."],[1087,"**`<output_dir>/experiment.md`** — the experiment-level mirror: the hypothesis\n(read from `ctx.config.metadata['hypothesis']` at `on_experiment_start`) and\nthe conclusion (from `ExperimentResult.conclusion` at `on_experiment_end`). So\nthe local mirror carries hypothesis + conclusion even with no dashboard."],[491,"**`algorithm.train(ctx) -> RunResult`** inside try/finally; on exception →\n`status=\"failed\"`. `backend.teardown(handles)` always runs in `finally`."],[586,"**`AliasMatcher`** — alias matching (predicted vs verified aliases)."],[980,"**`async build_batch(self, step_idx: int) -> TrainingBatch`**\nProduce the batch for `step_idx` (0-based). SFT slices its static datums; RL\nand SDFT roll out **on-policy** here. &#x2A;*The loss rides on the returned batch —\nthere is no separate loss override.** Returns a `TrainingBatch`."],[945,"**`async run(self, instruction: str, environment: BaseEnvironment, context: AgentContext) -> None`**\nThe core method — one rollout for one task. This is what you override."],[979,"**`async setup(self, ctx: RunContext, backend: TinkerBackend) -> None`**\nOne-time prep before the loop. Stash per-algorithm state on `self` (tokenized\ndatums for SFT; dataset + teacher client for SDFT/RL) and &#x2A;*must set\n`self._steps_per_epoch`**. The `backend` is the already-allocated LoRA\ntraining client; call `backend.get_tokenizer()`, `backend.save_for_sampler(...)`,\netc. Returns nothing."],[944,"**`async setup(self, environment: BaseEnvironment) -> None`** — one-time prep\nbefore any rollout, given the environment harbor allocated (the SDK default is\n`NoOpEnvironment`, a sandbox-free in-process env). Returns nothing."],[488,"**`backend.prepare(model=..., run_dir=...)`** → a dict of handles. &#x2A;If this\nraises, the run is recorded `status=\"failed\"` and returned early.*"],[1175,"**`close(self) -> None`** — flush and release resources at run end. After\nclose, the JSONL store refuses further writes."],[549,"**`combo`*&#x2A; chains phases (output of phase N feeds N+1); &#x2A;*`gepa_prompt`** does\nprompt search with no weight updates (needs the `gepa` extra)."],[1019,"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model (`extra=\"forbid\"`) describing\nthe backend's params. Whatever you put under `backend.params` in YAML is\nvalidated against this before the backend is constructed."],[1231,"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model (with `extra=\"forbid\"`)\ndescribing the transform's params. The factory validates the `params:` block\nfrom YAML against this model before constructing the transform, so an unknown\nor mistyped param fails loudly instead of being silently ignored."],[974,"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — a Pydantic model for the recipe's params,\nvalidated against `algorithm.params` in YAML."],[1263,"**`Config: ClassVar[type]`** — Pydantic model (`extra=\"forbid\"`) for the\nverifier's params; `params:` from YAML is validated against it."],[984,"**`data: list[tinker.Datum]`** — the step's training examples. The loss mask on\neach Datum decides which tokens are supervised (the algorithm's call, not the\ndataset's)."],[1232,"**`def __call__(self, rows: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]) -> Iterable[dict[str, Any]]`**\n— the one method. It receives `rows`, an iterable of plain dicts (one dict per\ndata row, exactly as read from the JSONL/parquet source or as emitted by the\nprevious transform), and returns an iterable of dicts. There is no fixed schema\non the dicts — keys are whatever your data has. The convention is **additive**:\nkeep the original keys and add new ones (`yield {**row, \"messages\": ...}`) so a\nlater transform or the algorithm can still see the source fields. Returning a\ngenerator is fine and encouraged — rows stream through lazily."],[1201,"**`def compute(self, task_rewards: Sequence[Sequence[float]]) -> float`** — the\none method. `task_rewards` is a sequence of sequences: **one inner sequence per\ntask**, holding that task's per-sample rewards. (So `task_rewards[i][j]` is the\nreward of sample `j` on task `i`.) It returns a single `float` — the aggregated\nscore for the benchmark. A sample is treated as \"passing\" when its reward\nclears `PASS_THRESHOLD` (`1.0`, defined in `metrics/basic.py`)."],[1264,"**`def verify(self, *, prompt: str, completion: str, target: dict[str, Any]) -> VerificationResult`**\n— all three arguments are **keyword-only**. `prompt` is the input text the\nmodel saw; `completion` is the model's generated text; `target` is a dict of\ngold/reference data for this example (answer keys, expected fields, etc.). It\nreturns a `VerificationResult` whose `reward` is a float and whose `info` is a\nfree-form dict of diagnostics (surfaced for debugging, not used for training)."],[568,"**`E2BVerifier`** (`e2b`) — `dockerfile`, `test_sh`, `test_state_py`. Runs the\nmodel output + tests inside an E2B sandbox; pass/fail from exit code."],[588,"**`EvalArtifacts` / `EvalSummary`** — result objects; `summary.retry_report`\ncarries `total_failures`."],[585,"**`evaluate_model(...)`** — score an `InferenceClient` (local/tinker/mock checkpoint)."],[34,"**`evsys_logger`** pushes the same record (metrics, predictions, hypothesis,\nconclusion) to the EvolvingSystems dashboard via `EVSYS_API_KEY` for a\ncentralized, cross-experiment history."],[1107,"**`exists(self, path: str) -> bool`** — return `True` if something is present\nat `path`, `False` otherwise. Callers use this to skip work or guard reads."],[1272,"**`expected: Any`** — the gold value from the task's `expected` field (string,\ndict, etc., depending on the fn)."],[721,"**`Experiment`*&#x2A; (OOP, with dashboard bookkeeping) wraps\n&#x2A;*`run_experiment(cfg)`** (the inner per-arm runner). Use `run_experiment`\ndirectly to train without bookkeeping."],[616,"**`ExperimentRun`** is a context-manager wrapper for the common flow:"],[590,"**`format_summary_markdown(summary, title=)`** — pretty summary."],[1132,"**`generate(self, *, prompt: str, max_tokens: int = 256, temperature: float = 0.0, stop: list[str] | None = None) -> str`**\n— synchronously generate text and return it as a string. **All arguments are\nkeyword-only** (note the leading `*`):"],[645,"**`InferenceClient`**: `generate(...)` — how eval/RL query a model."],[567,"**`InProcessVerifier`** (`in_process`) — `fn_name`, `expected`, `params`. A\nregistered Python fn called as `fn(completion, expected, **params)`. Sub-ms;\nuse for tool-call/exact match."],[328,"**`kind` + `params` envelopes.** Every pluggable block in the YAML is just a\nstring `kind` (a registry key) plus a free-form `params` dict. The runner\nlooks `kind` up in the matching registry and validates `params` against the\nregistered class's `.Config` Pydantic model. This indirection is what lets an\nevolution loop mutate YAML safely without importing typed classes."],[1108,"**`list(self, prefix: str) -> list[str]`** — return the paths under `prefix`.\nFor the local store, a directory prefix is walked recursively and a glob\npattern is expanded; paths come back relative to the store root."],[569,"**`LLMJudgeVerifier`** (`llm_judge`) — `judge_model`, `rubric`. Judge scores\nthe completion against the rubric."],[33,"**`local_logger`** writes per-step `metrics.jsonl` (train + val rows, split\ntagged), `predictions/`, a per-run `summary.md`, **and*&#x2A; an experiment-level\n**`experiment.md` containing the hypothesis and the final conclusion** — so the\nwhole research record lives on disk, no dashboard required."],[1174,"**`log_artifact(self, name: str, path: str, *, kind: str = \"file\") -> None`**\n— register a produced artifact under a logical `name` pointing at `path`. The\n`kind` argument is **keyword-only** and defaults to `\"file\"` (use it to mark\ne.g. `\"checkpoint\"`). Stores the pointer, not the bytes."],[1173,"**`log_hyperparams(self, params: dict[str, Any]) -> None`** — record the run's\nhyperparameters once. Values can be any JSON-serializable type, not just\nfloats. The JSONL store merges repeated calls into one file."],[1172,"**`log_metrics(self, metrics: dict[str, float], step: int, *, split: str = \"train\") -> None`**\n— record a whole dict of named metrics at `step`. The `split` argument is\n**keyword-only** (note the `*,`) and defaults to `\"train\"`. It tags which\nside of the train/val firewall the row belongs to: pass `split=\"val\"` for\nin-loop validation metrics so train and validation curves stay distinguishable\nin the same log. (The JSONL store writes `split` as a field on each row; the\nTensorBoard store ignores it because the split is already baked into the\nmetric keys like `val/loss`.)"],[1171,"**`log_scalar(self, key: str, value: float, step: int) -> None`** — record a\nsingle named scalar `value` at training `step`. The one-metric convenience\nform of `log_metrics`."],[493,"**`log_store.close()`** then **persist** `run_dir/run_result.json`\n(`run_id`, `status`, `metrics`, `artifacts`, `error`, `hparams`, `ts`)."],[490,"**`log_store.log_hyperparams(...)`** (experiment/run name, model, backend, tags)."],[1050,"**`LogContext`** — experiment-wide context shared across all hooks:\n`.output_dir`, `.config`, `.store`, `.run_key`, `.run_config`, `.group_name`,\n`.ids` (dashboard ids populated by logger callbacks), `.extras` (scratch shared\nbetween callbacks within a run)."],[1049,"**`LogState`** (called `LoopState` in code) — live training-loop state:\n`.step`, `.num_steps`, `.output_dir`, `.backend`, `.log_store`,\n`.checkpoint_mgr`, `.stop_requested`, `.ctx`. Call `state.request_stop()` from\nany loop hook to break the loop after the current step finishes."],[986,"**`loss_fn_config: dict[str, Any] | None`** — extra loss params; only used when\n`loss_fn` is a string."],[985,"**`loss_fn: tinker.types.LossFnType | LossCallable`** — *either* a\nserver-recognized string name (`\"cross_entropy\"`, `\"importance_sampling\"`, …)\nfor a server-side loss, *or* a Python callable for a client-side custom loss.\nThe loop dispatches the right backend method based on the type:\n`forward_backward_async` for a string, `forward_backward_custom_async` for a\ncallable. A `LossCallable` is `Callable[[model_output, batch_metadata], Any]`\nreturning a scalar tensor for the backward pass."],[643,"**`Metric`**: `compute(predictions, targets) -> float`."],[987,"**`metrics: dict[str, float]`** — algorithm-precomputed per-step metrics (e.g.\nreward stats, teacher entropy) merged into the per-step log row."],[1271,"**`model_output: str`** — the model's completion text."],[550,"**`multiplex`** log store fans out to N child stores; the runner auto-fills\neach `jsonl`/`tensorboard` child's `log_dir`."],[479,"**`name_template`** uses literal `{dotted.key}` placeholders (not\n`str.format`, so dots aren't attribute access) plus `{base}` = base run name.\nFloats are slugged (`1e-4` → `0p0001`-style via `%g`, `+`/`.` stripped)."],[1262,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key / YAML `kind`."],[973,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key and the YAML `algorithm.kind`."],[1200,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — registry key; the string you put on a benchmark's\n`metrics:` list."],[1131,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key / YAML `kind`."],[1170,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key / YAML `kind`."],[1018,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key, also the string you write under\n`backend.kind` in YAML (`\"tinker\"`, `\"local\"`, `\"mock\"`)."],[1102,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key, the string you put in YAML as\n`kind`. (Data stores have no `Config` ClassVar requirement in the protocol,\nbut the built-ins carry one — see below.)"],[1230,"**`name: ClassVar[str]`** — the registry key. This is the exact string you put\nas `kind:` in YAML."],[1062,"**`on_benchmark_eval(self, ctx: LogContext, eval_result: EvalResult, predictions: list[dict], *, step: int | None = None) -> None`**\n— per benchmark scored, in-loop (`step` = the train step) or post-training\n(`step=None`). `eval_result` carries metrics + breakdowns + tags; `predictions`\nis the per-task prediction rows. `step` is **keyword-only**."],[1056,"**`on_checkpoint(self, state: LoopState, row: ManifestRow) -> None`** — after each\ncheckpoint manifest row is recorded. `row` carries the checkpoint's name,\nstep, and paths. Useful for shipping/pruning checkpoints."],[1055,"**`on_eval(self, state: LoopState, step_idx: int, eval_name: str, metrics: dict[str, float]) -> None`**\n— once per evaluator after each in-loop eval. `eval_name` identifies the\nevaluator; `metrics` is its scalar output. Drives early stopping and val curves."],[1064,"**`on_experiment_end(self, ctx: LogContext, result: ExperimentResult) -> None`** —\nonce at experiment end. `result` carries `best_arm`, `best_score`, `status`,\n`conclusion`. Final summary / flush."],[1059,"**`on_experiment_start(self, ctx: LogContext) -> None`** — once at experiment\nstart, before any arm. A logger creates the experiment record here and sets\n`ctx.ids['experiment_id']`."],[1060,"**`on_group_start(self, ctx: LogContext, group_name: str) -> None`** — when a new\nrun-group is needed (`n_repeats` replicates or continual stages). A logger\ncreates the group → `ctx.ids[f'group:{group_name}']`."],[1063,"**`on_run_end(self, ctx: LogContext, run_result: RunResult, arm: ArmResult) -> None`**\n— per arm, after eval, before the run is marked completed. `run_result` is the\nalgorithm's result; `arm` is the arm record. Loggers close their sink and\nrecord final status here."],[1061,"**`on_run_start(self, ctx: LogContext) -> None`** — per arm, before training.\n`ctx.run_config` is set. A logger opens its run-scoped sink (e.g. `wandb.init`)\n→ `ctx.ids['run_id']`, reading the parent ids to link it."],[1054,"**`on_step_end(self, state: LoopState, step_idx: int, batch: TrainingBatch, metrics: dict[str, float]) -> None`**\n— after every train step's metric row is written. `step_idx` is the 0-based\nstep; `batch` is the step's training batch; `metrics` is that step's metric\ndict. The universal per-step hook."],[1057,"**`on_train_end(self, state: LoopState, artifacts: LoopArtifacts) -> None`** —\nonce after the loop completes (including the final checkpoint save).\n`artifacts` carries totals (requested steps, train seconds, run dir,\ncheckpoints). Flush summaries, close files."],[1053,"**`on_train_start(self, state: LoopState) -> None`** — once, before the for-loop\nstarts. Open log files, init a wandb run, snapshot config."],[1273,"**`params: dict`** — the task's `params` block, a plain dict of options."],[1020,"**`prepare(self, *, model: dict[str, Any], run_dir: str) -> dict[str, Any]`**\nCalled once before training. Both arguments are keyword-only."],[1105,"**`read_json(self, path: str) -> Any`** — read a single JSON document at\n`path` and return the parsed value (any JSON type — dict, list, scalar)."],[1103,"**`read_jsonl(self, path: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]`** — read a JSONL file\nat `path` and return its rows as a list of dicts, one dict per line. This is\nthe primary way datasets are loaded."],[589,"**`RetryReport` / `RetryFailure` / `call_with_retry`** — the retry layer."],[862,"**`run_every` controls *when* it's scored.** `run_every: N` scores the\nbenchmark **in-loop every N steps** during training; omit `run_every` and it's\nscored **once, after training**. (This is true of any entry — a `test`\nbenchmark can have a `run_every` and run in-loop too.)"],[27,"**`run_every`** decides *when* an entry is scored: `run_every: N` scores it\n**in-loop every N steps**; omit `run_every` and it's scored **once, after\ntraining**. This applies to any entry."],[497,"**`RunContext`** — everything an algorithm needs:\n`run_id`, `output_dir`, `config` (the parsed `ExperimentConfig`), `data_store`,\n`log_store`, `backend`, `extras: dict` (free bag — e.g. `train_rows`,\n`backend_handles`, tinker `training_client`)."],[498,"**`RunResult`** — what `train` returns:\n`run_id`, `status` (`\"completed\"|\"failed\"|\"cancelled\"`),\n`metrics: dict[str,float]`, `artifacts: dict[str,str]` (e.g.\n`{\"final_checkpoint\": \"s3://…\"}`), `error: str?`, `extras: dict`."],[587,"**`score_rows(...)` / `ModelEvalConfig`** — generic scorer + eval config."],[40,"**`set-up-research-project`** — scaffold a repo into the standard\n`data/ · src/ · experiments/ · .evsys/` layout."],[863,"**`split` (`val` / `test`) is just a label** — it namespaces the metrics so\ndifferent benchmarks' scores stay apart in the logs; it does *not* decide when\nan entry runs. `pass@1` here = the fraction of tasks whose answer the verifier\naccepts (contains the right `<answer>SLUG</answer>`)."],[28,"**`split`** (`val` / `test`) is just a **label** that namespaces the metrics so\ndifferent benchmarks' scores stay apart in the logs — it does *not* decide\nwhen an entry runs. A `test` benchmark can run in-loop too; just give it a\n`run_every`."],[981,"**`step_metrics(self, step_idx: int, batch: TrainingBatch, fb_result: Any) -> dict[str, float]`*&#x2A;\n&#x2A;(Optional, defaults to `{}`.)* Per-step metrics computed from the\nforward-backward result. `fb_result` is what the backend's\n`forward_backward_*_async()` future resolved to; inspect\n`fb_result.loss_fn_outputs` (one entry per Datum) to derive, e.g., `train_mean_nll`."],[1024,"**`teardown(self, handles: dict[str, Any]) -> None`**\nCalled once after training to release whatever `prepare` allocated. `handles`\nis exactly the dict `prepare` returned. Returns nothing. (`MockBackend` and\n`TinkerBackend` no-op here; `LocalBackend` drops the model and empties the\nCUDA/MPS cache.)"],[975,"**`train(self, ctx: RunContext) -> RunResult`** — execute one full run."],[688,"**`Transform`**"],[41,"**`using-the-sdk`** — author correct configs, transforms, and algorithms."],[499,"**`VerificationResult`** — `reward: float`, `info: dict`."],[644,"**`Verifier`**: `verify(prompt, completion, target) -> reward` (RL reward or\nper-task scoring)."],[943,"**`version(self) -> str | None`** — an optional version string (`\"1.0.0\"`)."],[1106,"**`write_json(self, path: str, value: Any) -> None`** — serialize `value` to\nJSON and write it to `path`. Used for manifests, summaries, config snapshots."],[1104,"**`write_jsonl(self, path: str, rows: Iterable[dict[str, Any]]) -> None`** —\nwrite an iterable of dicts to `path`, one JSON object per line. Used for\nrendered training data, predictions, and other row-shaped outputs. Returns\nnothing."],[661,"**① Experiment**"],[664,"**② Data**"],[667,"**③ Algorithm**"],[670,"**④ Evaluation**"],[673,"**⑤ Extensibility**"],[194,"**Agent harnesses** — train a model *inside* your own multi-turn harness (any\nharbor `BaseAgent`) so it learns to use your tools — the way Opus is trained\ninside the Claude Code harness."],[183,"**Algorithmic changes** — only the heavy math: override `build_batch()` and the loss."],[531,"**algorithms**"],[193,"**Algorithms** — any recipe under the sun (SFT, RL, distillation, or your\nown), LoRA on any model — defined by overriding a single `build_batch()`."],[486,"**Apply transforms** in order (`_apply_transforms`); each transform is called\nas `transform(rows) -> rows`."],[593,"**Auth:** requires an API key + project id by default; missing creds raise\n`EvsysAuthError` unless offline mode is on."],[478,"**Axis keys are dotted paths** into the run dict (`_set_dotted`)."],[126,"**Backend-pluggable** — same YAML can run locally on TRL or remotely on\nTinker; backends are interchangeable."],[189,"**Backends & compute** — mock / local / tinker, rollouts via Harbor."],[548,"**Backends route by `(recipe, backend)`**: pick `mock` for tests, `local` for\nTRL+PEFT on your GPU, `tinker` for hosted training."],[533,"**backends**"],[640,"**Benchmark** — the *test set*, scored **once after** training. Model\nselection must never key off it."],[487,"**Build algorithm** from the registry with `run.algorithm.params`."],[484,"**Build backend** from `run.backend`."],[483,"**Build stores** from the top-level specs. For `jsonl`/`tensorboard` log\nstores (and `multiplex` children), `log_dir` is auto-filled to\n`<run_dir>/logs[/kind]` if not set."],[201,"**Callbacks** — hook the training lifecycle for logging, early stopping, or\ndashboard upload."],[2903,"**CE distillation** — train the student to match the teacher's\nrenormalized top-K distribution at each position via cross\\_entropy."],[187,"**Checkpointing & artifacts.**"],[619,"**Config models:** `ExperimentConfig`, `RunConfig`, `AlgorithmConfig`,\n`DataConfig`, `ModelConfig`, `BackendConfig`, `EvalConfig`, `DataStoreSpec`,\n`LogStoreSpec`, `MetricSpec`, `VerifierSpec`, `TransformSpec`, `InferenceSpec`."],[489,"**Construct `RunContext`** carrying stores, backend, and an `extras` dict\n(`train_rows`, `n_train_rows`, `backend_handles`, `model_name`, `tags`)."],[625,"**Dashboard:** `DashboardClient`, `ExperimentRun`, `DashboardClientError`,\n`EvsysAuthError`."],[200,"**Data & log stores** — where data is read and where metrics/artifacts are\nwritten (local files, the dashboard, TensorBoard)."],[182,"**Data ablations** — what data goes into training (sources, mixes, transforms)."],[693,"**data only — no supervision encoded**"],[624,"**Data shapes:** `TargetFormat`, `ChatMessagesRow`, `HarborTask`,\n`PromptExample`, the three verifier specs + `VerifierPayload`, block helpers,\n`detect_format`, `from_dict`, `to_dict`, `iter_jsonl`."],[185,"**Data** — loading, caching & lineage → data format rows."],[543,"**data\\_stores**"],[127,"**Decoupled storage** — the library imports zero Supabase code by default;\nSupabase is an optional adapter."],[202,"**Deployers** — ship the trained adapter (e.g. Fireworks) with one line."],[594,"**Env vars** (`constants.py`):"],[492,"**Eval (best-effort)** — only if `status == \"completed\"`. Any eval exception\nis logged and swallowed; **eval never fails the run**. Eval metrics are\nmerged into `result.metrics` under `eval/<metric_kind>` keys and logged."],[188,"**Evaluation** — in-loop validation + benchmark scoring, metrics & verifiers."],[654,"**Expands** the config — a single `run`, a list of `runs`, or a `matrix`\nshorthand — into one or more **arms** (each arm is one `RunConfig` = one\ntraining job). `n_repeats` replicates an arm across seeds for variance."],[184,"**Experiment orchestration** — sweeps, arms, seeds, failure isolation, conclusions."],[1058,"**Experiment-scope hooks** (dispatched by the `Experiment`, not the loop — these\nlet one logger own the full lifecycle, threading dashboard ids through\n`ctx.ids`):"],[707,"**Experiment** — the top-level study. `Experiment.from_yaml(...).run()` owns\ndashboard experiment/run creation, sweep expansion, per-arm failure\nisolation, post-train scoring, metric forwarding, and conclusion building."],[1894,"**Flat** (`tinker_cookbook`'s native `metrics.jsonl`)::"],[325,"**From Python:**"],[324,"**From YAML (canonical interface):**"],[710,"**Hypothesis → success\\_metric → conclusion** — the hypothesis is the\nquestion; `success_metric` ranks arms into `best_arm`; the `conclusion`\nsummarizes the outcome. All recorded on the dashboard."],[199,"**Inference clients** — how eval / RL query a model to generate."],[539,"**inference**"],[485,"**Load rows** via `_load_rows` (dispatch on `source_kind`)."],[545,"**log\\_stores**"],[190,"**Logging, dashboard & storage.**"],[626,"**Logging:** `configure_logger`, `get_logger`, `set_level`."],[1052,"**Loop-scope hooks** (dispatched by the `TrainingLoop`):"],[1205,"**Macro** mean reward: for each task take the mean of its samples, then average those task-means. Empty tasks are skipped; returns `0.0` if there are none."],[535,"**metrics**"],[197,"**Metrics** — score rollouts however you measure success: `pass@1`, `pass@3`,\ncost, latency, your own."],[1209,"**Micro** pass rate: total passing samples ÷ total samples, pooled across all tasks (`0.0` if no samples)."],[125,"**Modular** — adding a new algorithm/verifier/metric is a decorator + a\nPydantic Config class. No library fork."],[1892,"**Nested** (the SDK's own `log_store` output)::"],[781,"**No transform is needed here.** A row with `task_id` + `instruction` +\n`verifier` is *already* a `HarborTask`, so the SDK detects the format directly.\n(If your raw data were plain QA, you'd write a `@register_transform` that builds\nthese task dicts — same idea as SFT's `jsonl_to_chat`.)"],[816,"**No transform is needed** — `{inputs: {question}, expected}` is already a\n`PromptExample`, so the SDK detects the format directly. (As always, you could\nwrite a `@register_transform` if your raw data came in a different shape.)"],[2723,"**One Datum per assistant turn** — a single-turn trajectory yields one\nDatum, a multi-turn one yields one per turn, all carrying the same\ntrajectory-level advantage. Each Datum carries:"],[330,"**One registry per extension point**, each with its own decorator and Python\nentry-point group, so external packages auto-extend the registries on import."],[656,"**Picks the best arm** by your `success_metric` and records an\n`ExperimentResult` (`best_arm`, `conclusion`, metrics)."],[620,"**Protocols & run types:** `Algorithm`, `Backend`, `DataStore`, `LogStore`,\n`Metric`, `Verifier`, `Transform`, `InferenceClient`, `RunContext`, `RunResult`."],[329,"**Protocols, not base classes.** Extensions satisfy a `typing.Protocol`\n(PEP 544) — any class with the right methods works; no subclassing the\nlibrary, so a third-party extension never has to \"import the world.\""],[578,"**Registry behavior:** duplicate keys raise unless the same class;\n`register(name)` also sets `cls.name = name`; `get` raises a `KeyError` listing\navailable keys. `schema_for(kind, name)` returns the `.Config`'s\n`model_json_schema()` — this is exactly what an evolution loop reads to learn the\nlegal mutation space."],[622,"**Registry:** `register_*` / `get_*` / `list_*` for all 8 kinds."],[1274,"**returns `float`** — the reward, typically `1.0` (pass) or `0.0` (fail)."],[977,"**Returns** a `RunResult`: `run_id`, `status` (`\"completed\"`/`\"failed\"`/\n`\"cancelled\"`), `metrics` (final scalars), `artifacts` (named paths, e.g.\n`{\"run_dir\": ..., \"checkpoint-final\": ...}`), and an optional `error` string."],[1023,"**Returns** a dict of backend-specific *handles* that the runner attaches to\n`ctx.extras[\"backend_handles\"]`. The algorithm reads from it — e.g. a tinker\nrun needs `{\"backend\": \"tinker\", \"service_client\": ..., \"model_name\": ...,\n\"renderer_name\": ..., \"run_dir\": ...}`; a local run needs\n`{\"model\": <hf_model>, \"tokenizer\": ..., ...}`. The keys are a private\ncontract between a backend and the algorithms that target it."],[709,"**Run group** — `n_repeats > 1` replicates an arm across seeds (shared\n`group_id`) so variance is a config field, not a bespoke script."],[623,"**Runner:** `run_experiment`."],[655,"**Runs each arm** through the same pipeline — **Data → Training →\nEvaluation** — with per-arm failure isolation."],[579,"**Same pattern** for every point: `register_verifier`, `register_metric`,\n`register_backend`, `register_inference`, `register_transform`,\n`register_data_store`, `register_log_store`."],[124,"**Single declarative YAML** drives a full experiment (data → train → eval),\nso an evolutionary algorithm can mutate it without writing Python."],[2900,"**Student rollout** — sample from the live student weights on the user\nquestion (no demo). Each sample is a completion + per-position logprobs."],[2901,"**Teacher prompt** — build a frozen-teacher prompt that contains the\ngolden answer as an in-context demonstration."],[2902,"**Teacher topK** — append the student completion to the teacher prompt,\nask the teacher for its top-K token distribution at each completion\nposition via tinker's `topk_prompt_logprobs` sampling API."],[1257,"**The `Verifier` class registry** — full plugin classes (`name` + `Config` +\n`verify(...)`), registered with `@register_verifier` and selected by `kind:`.\nThis is the general extension point."],[1258,"**The in-process verifier-fn registry** — plain Python *functions* that live\ninside the SDK and are referenced **by name from task data**. A `HarborTask`\ncarries `verifier: {kind: in_process, fn_name: ...}`, and `fn_name` resolves\nto one of these functions. The remote backend never stores verifier *code* —\nonly the `fn_name` plus per-task `expected`/`params`."],[681,"**The SDK handles:** loading, pull/cache-by-id with lineage (`Workspace`),\nrunning transforms in order, and the strict `parse_rows` conversion."],[186,"**The training loop** — forward/backward, optimizer steps, save cadence."],[192,"**Tinker-compatible backends** — train on anything that exposes the Tinker\ntraining server: Fireworks, TML, SkyRL, … one line in the config switches provider."],[708,"**Training run (arm)** — one `RunConfig` = one concrete training job (one\ncell of a sweep). `runs` / `matrix` produce many arms."],[537,"**transforms**"],[195,"**Transforms** — turn any raw data into the standard data-format rows; chain\nbuilt-ins or register your own."],[198,"**Validation & evaluation** — score against benchmarks via `metadata.benchmark`:\n`run_every: N` scores in-loop every N steps (omit it to score once after\ntraining); the `split` tag (`val`/`test`) just separates the metrics."],[641,"**Validation** — scored **in-loop** every N steps to drive selection."],[541,"**verifiers**"],[196,"**Verifiers** — the reward / correctness check for RL and eval\n(`exact_match`, `contains`, LLM-judge, or 