r. There's no `Config`; a metric takes no params:"],[2691,"The convention matches tinker\\_cookbook: `(step + 1) % save_every == 0`.\nDisabled when `save_every == 0`."],[854,"The conversation carries **only data** — it does *not* say which tokens to learn\nfrom. That's the algorithm's decision (next step)."],[2919,"The cookbook does the same step inline; here it's a named function so\nthe :class:`~evsys_sdk.algorithms.sdft.SDFT` algorithm and tests\nshare the implementation."],[2905,"The cookbook's default demonstration template. Researchers usually\noverride this in the algorithm config (e.g. to bracket the golden answer\nin `\\<answer>...\\</answer>` tags)."],[2890,"The data interface the SDFT algorithm consumes per step."],[679,"The data surface standardizes *anything* into a few typed shapes, then hands\nthose to the algorithm. Tokenization and supervision live **below** this\nboundary — the typed rows carry only data; the algorithm decides what's a\ntarget token."],[2913,"The Datum is what :func:`build_topk_targets` consumes: it carries the\nfull sequence as `model_input` and a per-position mask indicating\nwhich positions are completion tokens (the ones the teacher scores)."],[2688,"The decision policy is intentionally tiny — `should_save(step)` returns\nTrue every `save_every` steps (after the optimizer step at that index).\nThe actual save call is dispatched by the loop, which has the live\n`Backend` handle; the manager only records the resulting paths."],[941,"The default harness is `BasicLoopAgent` in\n`src/evsys_sdk/training/harbor_agents.py`. It subclasses `BaseAgent` from\n`harbor.agents.base`, which the rollout engine builds fresh per trial. The\nmethods a harbor `BaseAgent` implements (as `BasicLoopAgent` shows):"],[275,"The design target is an **evolutionary optimization loop** that mutates the YAML\nwithout writing Python: each extension exposes a Pydantic `Config` whose JSON\nschema defines the legal mutation space."],[966,"The easy path: `BaseAlgorithm`"],[730,"The eight registries"],[494,"The eval loop (`_run_eval`) builds the inference client from\n`eval.inference`, generates for each row (prompt = `row[\"prompt\"]` or the last\nmessage content), extracts `<answer>…</answer>` if present, and compares against\ntargets (`tool_slug`/`answer` + `toolkit`) using each configured `Metric`."],[1935,"The expansion is the single source of truth for both the YAML `matrix:`\nloader and programmatic builds (the legacy `_expand_matrix` delegates here)."],[650,"The Experiment — the organizing unit"],[2627,"The experiment-wide :class:`LogContext` (shared with the Experiment-scope\nhooks). `None` for a bare `run_experiment` with no Experiment driving it;\npopulated when the Experiment threads callbacks into the loop."],[2624,"The fields are mutated in-place by the loop as the run progresses;\n`step` advances every iteration, `stop_requested` flips when a\ncallback calls :meth:`request_stop`. Other fields are immutable for\nthe run's lifetime."],[651,"The five layers"],[2702,"The format is intentionally identical to the manifest tinker\\_cookbook used\nto emit, so downstream consumers (e.g.\n:meth:`~evsys_sdk.inference.tinker.TinkerInference.from_run_result`) keep\nworking unchanged when an algorithm is ported to the native loop."],[1896,"The forwarder normalizes both into a `dict[str, float]` via\n:func:`_extract_metrics` before pushing."],[725,"The four-step contract"],[2616,"The framework owns only :attr:`run_key` (the local output-dir name). All\ndashboard ids (`experiment_id` / `group:\\<name>` / `run_id`) are\ncallback-owned and accumulate on :attr:`ids` as the `create_*` hooks\nfire. Arms run sequentially, so `ids[\"run_id\"]` is the current arm's."],[1732,"The full experiment is described by ExperimentConfig, which is what gets\nserialized to and from YAML. Each block uses a `kind:` discriminator that\nselects the matching registry entry; the registered class's `.Config` model\nvalidates the rest of that block."],[240,"The full hand-written reference for configs, CLI, and protocols."],[1835,"The full parsed ExperimentConfig (kept generic to avoid circular import)."],[1611,"The full training-state path (weights + optimizer) of an arm's final\ncheckpoint. Continual learning loads *weights only* from this into the\nnext stage. Distinct from :meth:`_final_checkpoint`, which returns the\ninference-only sampler path."],[2973,"The functions here return `tinker.ModelInput` so they're drop-in for any\nsampling / forward call."],[2760,"The harbor sampler for this rollout. `model_client` picks it:\n`\"tinker\"` → on-policy `TinkerLLM` (needs `model_path`);\n`\"litellm\"` → harbor's litellm LLM for any provider (`model_name` a\nlitellm string, e.g. `\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-1\"`; keys from the\nprovider env vars)."],[1400,"The harbor upload body lives in `_harbor_upload.upload_harbor` (reusable for\nother harbor-format entities) — this module only wires the benchmark store\nmethods and keeps the historical `UploadResult` shape."],[154,"The high-level path is one class with declarative inputs:"],[2455,"The interface is one method::"],[162,"The legacy `run_experiment(cfg)` is still the inner runner that\n`Experiment` calls per arm — bypass `Experiment` only when you need to do\ntraining without dashboard bookkeeping."],[74,"The library defines `DataStore` and `LogStore` as protocols (see\n`src/evsys_sdk/protocols.py`). Built-in implementations:"],[1109,"The local filesystem store is the default; you almost never name it explicitly.\nWhen you do, it looks like this:"],[2171,"The loop already merges `batch.metrics` (teacher entropy / truncated\ncount); here we add the loss derived from the forward-backward output.\nPer-position student logprobs are 0 on non-loss positions, negative on\nthe rest; ignore the zeros."],[2959,"The loop fires forward\\_backward / optim WITHOUT awaiting, then awaits each\none's `result_async()` (the shape :class:`MockBackend` implements). But\ntinker's `forward_backward_async` / `optim_step_async` are *coroutine\nfunctions* — calling them returns an un-awaited coroutine, not a future.\nThis wraps that coroutine so `await wrapper.result_async()` awaits the\ncoroutine to obtain the tinker future, then awaits the future's result."],[2856,"The loop owns:"],[2876,"The metrics / prediction builders are pure functions over\n:class:`TrajectoryGroup`\\s — harbor-free and directly testable."],[25,"The model then trains **inside that harness** — taking turns, calling your\ntools, getting rewarded on the outcome — so it **learns to use the harness\nitself**. This is exactly how Opus is trained inside the Claude Code harness:\nregister your harness, and the model you train learns to operate in it. The\nagent harness is the third lever."],[871,"the model's actual answer for each val task each time it's scored"],[796,"the model's actual rollout for each val task"],[2828,"The only thing each algorithm overrides."],[662,"The organizing unit — a hypothesis, one or more runs, an auto-synthesized conclusion."],[703,"The organizing unit — a hypothesis, one or more training runs, and an auto-synthesized conclusion."],[2751,"The other half of the wiring is :func:`build_in_loop_evaluators` — a\nmetadata-aware factory that the three native algorithm composers call to\nturn `metadata.benchmark` list entries with a `run_every` field into\n:class:`BenchmarkEvaluator` instances ready for the\n:class:`~evsys_sdk.training.loop.TrainingLoop` evaluators list."],[2821,"The output directory written to. Algorithms surface this as\n`RunResult.artifacts[\"run_dir\"]` for downstream consumers\n(e.g. `TinkerInference.from_run_result`)."],[731,"The payoff"],[935,"The pluggable rollout harness the policy is trained inside, so it learns to use that harness."],[2750,"The post-training scoring path (`Experiment._eval_arm` →\n`Benchmark.score(client)`) takes a *synchronous* `InferenceClient`.\nThe training-loop eval slot hands evaluators a live *async*\n`SamplingClient`.