ut forking the SDK."],[311,"the respective SDK"],[1137,"The return is the generated completion as a plain `str`."],[2791,"The reward is produced by harbor running our\n:class:`~evsys_sdk.training.harbor_agents.EvsysVerifier` (the job-level verifier)\n**host-side, no container**: it wraps the task's registered verifier fn over the\ncompletion the agent wrote. SHARED verifier mode (the default) keeps it in the\nagent's no-op environment; the dummy `tests/test.sh` only satisfies harbor's\ntask-load check and is never executed. (Generation-only rollouts disable the\nverifier and use `environment_mode=\"separate\"` so no `test.sh` is needed.)"],[2996,"The rollout data model — one shape for all (multi-turn) rollouts."],[281,"The run lifecycle"],[1491,"The runner builds the container per the `dockerfile`, drops in the\nmodel's completion + `test_state.py`, executes `test_sh` (default\n`pytest -q test_state.py`), and reads pass/fail from the exit code."],[1506,"The runner calls the judge model with the rubric + completion and parses a\nnumeric score from the response (usually in a `\\boxed\\{\\}` or\n`\\<score>...\\</score>` tag)."],[1501,"The runner looks up `fn_name` in a registered verifier-fn map and calls\nit with `(completion, expected, **params)`. Sub-millisecond — use this\nfor tool-call matching, exact-match, boxed-answer parsing."],[878,"The runner uses `Experiment(cfg).run()` (not the bare `run_experiment`) so the\n`local_logger` callback fires and writes the files above — including\n`experiment.md` with the hypothesis and conclusion."],[2626,"The same log\\_store the loop writes to. Callbacks can also write\nauxiliary rows (e.g. `log_metrics(\\{\"debug/x\": 1\\}, step=...)`)."],[1516,"The schemas runners consume and dashboards render. Mirrors the production\ninternal types so JSONL files round-trip between this SDK and the internal\nserving / dashboard stack without conversion."],[629,"The SDK **flattens** that into generic `kind`+`params` Pydantic envelopes\nresolved against registries at load time, so an evolution loop can mutate YAML\nwithout importing the typed classes."],[1950,"The SDK holds **no Supabase service key**. Every call routes through the\nbackend gateway (`POST \\{API\\}/api/dashboard/api/sdk/data/`) authenticated by the\nuser's Bearer API key; the backend validates the key, checks the user is a\nmember of the relevant project, runs the op with its service key, and returns\nthe data. Same method surface as before — only the transport changed."],[627,"The SDK is the **external, declarative front end** to the production training\nstack in `backend/api/experiments/`:"],[849,"The SDK reads the file through a **data store** and hands the rows to the next\nstage. At this point they're still raw dicts — `{\"query\": ..., \"tool_slug\": ...}`."],[1764,"The SDK root logger is named `evsys_sdk`; per-module loggers\nobtained via :func:`get_logger` propagate to it."],[630,"The SDK's `data_types.py` mirrors **only** the row/verifier shapes\n(`ChatMessagesRow`, `HarborTask`, `PromptExample`, the three verifiers) so\nJSONL round-trips between the two stacks without conversion."],[631,"The SDK's run-result types (`RunContext`, `RunResult`, `VerificationResult`)\nlive in `protocols.py` rather than as an `Experiment` campaign object."],[2899,"The Self-Distillation Fine-Tuning algorithm (Shenfeld et al., 2026):"],[1347,"The single resolver shared by the experiment config, the standalone\n`run_benchmark`, and the CLI — so all accept the same references:"],[2824,"The step horizon passed to :meth:`TrainingLoop.run` (`num_steps`) —\nNOT the number of steps actually executed. These differ when a callback\nearly-stops the loop via `state.request_stop()`: this field still reads\nthe requested ceiling. For \"how many steps actually ran\", read\n`state.step + 1` inside `on_train_end` (`state.step` is the last\nexecuted index)."],[820,"The student is **CE-distilled** toward that teacher distribution."],[830,"the student's answer for each val question"],[2910,"The teacher gets to see the golden answer as a soft hint in the user\nturn (via `demo_template`). Student completions then get appended to\nthis prompt for teacher-forced top-K scoring."],[978,"The Tinker-backed recipes don't reimplement `train`. They subclass\n`BaseAlgorithm` (`src/evsys_sdk/algorithms/base.py`), which owns the whole\ncomposer body and **is itself the StepBuilder** the loop drives. A concrete\nalgorithm overrides just the per-recipe pieces:"],[1608,"The trained sampler checkpoint URI from the arm's artifacts."],[964,"The training recipe — SFT, RL, distillation, or any custom loss — that decides what each batch contains."],[2716,"The two-step pipeline:"],[2172,"The user turn the student sees (no demo). The harbor agent's\nTinkerLLM renders it into a chat-templated prompt internally."],[649,"The whole system at a glance — one ExperimentConfig, five layers, eight registries."],[1977,"The workspace root (`$EVSYS_WORKSPACE` or `./.evsys`) writes a\nself-ignoring `.gitignore` (`*`) on init, so nothing in it is ever tracked.\nRows are written **raw** (D17); `MaterializedDataset` carries the dataset's\n`format` + `transform` so the trainer can render typed rows on read."],[2965,"The wrapper is thin — every method is a one-to-one passthrough to the\nunderlying tinker client, plus the one ergonomic affordance of returning\na wrapped :class:`TinkerSamplingClient` from\n`snapshot_sampling_client` (so callers don't have to know about the\nsampler URI machinery)."],[2006,"The YAML is canonical — Python builders just emit the same dict tree."],[130,"The YAML loader knows which registry to look up `kind:` in based on the\nsurrounding context. No string-prefix tricks."],[279,"The YAML schema (config models)"],[1286,"Then a task can reference it: `verifier: {kind: in_process, fn_name: startswith, expected: \"Answer:\", params: {ignore_case: true}}`."],[856,"Then add `{ kind: strip_pii, params: { field: query } }` to `transforms`. The\nSDK finds it in the registry by that name. See Extensibility."],[2654,"Then hand to the loop:"],[1186,"Then in YAML:"],[1089,"Then list it on the experiment:"],[1117,"Then reference it by `kind` in YAML — no SDK edit:"],[1156,"Then reference it by `kind`:"],[1240,"Then reference it by its registered name in YAML:"],[215,"Then run the no-GPU, no-network hello world:"],[817,"There's no teacher model to configure — it's &#x2A;*built automatically from\n`model.name`**. Each step:"],[951,"There's one built-in harness; you select an alternative by pointing the RL\nalgorithm at any harbor agent's import path:"],[167,"These all extend the same protocol surface and should arrive incrementally\nwithout breaking changes to the public API."],[1269,"These are **functions**, not classes, and they live in\n`src/evsys_sdk/verifiers/fns.py`. They are the single source of truth for cheap\nPython verification logic. A task references one by name:"],[1525,"These are *data shapes* (Pydantic / dataclasses) describing the verification\nplan; the runtime `Verifier` Protocol in `protocols.py` is what actually\nEXECUTES verification. They are deliberately separate concepts."],[2772,"These subclass harbor base classes, so `harbor` is imported at module top.\nOur own code **never imports this module directly** — harbor loads these by the\nstring `import_path` recorded in the job/agent config at runtime (see\n:mod:`evsys_sdk.training.harbor_engine`). That keeps the optional `[harbor]`\nextra out of the base import path."],[1917,"Third-party packages can also register via Python entry points; see\n`_entry_points.py` for the loader."],[845,"This is a full walkthrough for someone who has never used the SDK. We'll train a\nsmall model to pick the right tool for a user's query — emitting\n`<answer>TOOL_SLUG</answer>` — and explain **every** moving part: the raw data,\nthe transform that shapes it, the built-in algorithm, in-loop validation, and\nwhere the logs land."],[2602,"This is the \"callbacks own the store\" mode: construct `Experiment` WITHOUT\na `store=` (so the orchestrator makes no store calls) and add this\ncallback instead. If `Experiment` already has a store (`ctx.store` set),\nthis callback disables itself to avoid double-writing. The store handle is\nbuilt lazily from the environment (EvsysStore) unless one is injected\n(`cb._store = ...`) — the test seam."],[782,"This is the heart of RL. Each task carries an **in-process verifier**:"],[988,"This is the seam for **any loss**: focal loss, DPO, GRPO, a custom RL objective —\noverride `build_batch`, set the `loss_fn`, and the shared loop drives it."],[2934,"This is the shape tinker's server-side `cross_entropy` loss consumes;\nsee `training_client.forward_backward_async(loss_fn=\"cross_entropy\")`."],[1546,"This is the standardized boundary between the transform stage and a\nStepBuilder/algorithm: `raw rows -> transforms -> parse_rows(fmt) -> typed\nrows`. `fmt` is a :class:`TargetFormat` (or its string value). Every row\nmust match `fmt` per :func:`detect_format`; a mismatch raises\n`ValueError` naming the offending row — no silent coercion, mirroring the\nSDK's `extra='forbid'` philosophy. Tokenization/rollout stays downstream,\nowned by the algorithm."],[177,"This is the whole point of `evsys-sdk`: &#x2A;*turn your favourite coding agent into\na model lab.**"],[1932,"This is what an experiment script reaches for instead of writing a per-axis\n`for` loop. Sweep + Experiment together let `run.py` stay declarative:"],[2904,"This module owns Step 4's data shaping (turning teacher responses into\n`tinker.Datum` objects with `(N, K)`-shaped target\\_tokens + weights)\nplus the teacher-prompt helper for Step 2. The\n:class:`~evsys_sdk.algorithms.sdft.SDFT` algorithm orchestrates 1-4."],[14,"This page walks through the whole loop: **writing your own experiments with\nClaude Code** (or any coding agent). The agent reads what's been tried, launches\na new training run on Tinker, scores it, records what happened, and iterates —\ntoward a small model that beats frontier on your task at a fraction of the cost."],[225,"This takes you from a zero-setup **mock** wiring test to **real** local\ntraining — no GPU required. The config shape is identical; you only swap the\n`backend`."],[230,"This writes a real `adapter_model.safetensors` (the trained LoRA), per-step\n`metrics.jsonl`, and a resumable `checkpoint-5/` under\n`examples/quickstart_experiment/outputs/`. Bump `max_steps` to 100–500 for a\nreal run, or set `backend.kind: tinker` to train hosted."],[1650,"Thread-safe filesystem mirror for experiments and generations."],[2658,"Three built-ins ship today:"],[1983,"Three concerns, three modules:"],[1573,"Three forms supported:"],[327,"Three ideas hold it together:"],[2034,"tinker"],[3009,"tinker"],[1718,"Tinker chat renderer hint, e.g. 'qwen3'."],[443,"Tinker chat renderer hint, e.g. `qwen3`"],[1417,"Tinker SFT/RL (and any other algorithm that follows the same convention)\nappends one JSON row per saved checkpoint to `\\<output_dir>/checkpoints.jsonl`:"],[2513,"Tinker streams logits/logprobs back, the callable runs locally on\neach Datum, and the returned scalar gets sent back for the backward\npass. This is the same hook SDFT uses for analytical reverse-KL,\nexposed here as a first-class extension point."],[2960,"tinker_backend"],[15,"Tinker-protocol infrastructure already made the hard part — GPUs, sharding, the\ntraining loop — someone else's problem. What's left is *research*: which **data**\nand which **recipe** win. That's the only thing the agent touches."],[179,"Tinker-protocol training infrastructure has made the hard part — provisioning\nGPUs, sharding, the training loop — someone else's problem. What's left is the\n*research*: which **data** and which **recipe** produce a model that wins on\nyour task. `evsys-sdk` makes that research the only thing you (and your agent)\ntouch, and standardizes + centralizes every experiment so the agent always has\nthe context of what's been tried."],[2550,"Tinker-style future with `.result_async()` resolving to a value."],[2942,"Tinker's CE loss is left-shifted (predicts position `t` from position\n`t-1`), so `model_input` covers positions `[0, N-1]`, `target_tokens`\ncovers `[1, N]`, and `weights` aligns with `target_tokens`."],[2188,"Tinker's cross\\_entropy loss returns `loss_fn_outputs[i][\"logprobs\"]`:\na per-position vector of log-probabilities of the target token (a\n\"perfect\" prediction has logprob 0; otherwise negative). The mean NLL\nis `-sum(logprob * weight) / sum(weight)` over the loss-mask\npositions, averaged across the batch."],[2523,"Tinker's own `ForwardBackwardOutput` is opaque (pydantic with no public\nattrs in the installed version), so consumers go through the loss\\_fn\\_outputs\nfield on the actual response. The Protocol here lists what the loop reads\nso the contract is explicit; MockBackend constructs duck-typed objects."],[2969,"Tinker's save\\_\\*\\_async result envelopes carry a `.path` attribute\n(verified against cookbook usage in distillation/sdft.py:739, where the\nsame dotted access ships)."],[2027,"TinkerBackend"],[2943,"TinkerBackend"],[2961,"TinkerBackend — concrete :class:`~evsys_sdk.training.backend.Backend`\nimplementation against `tinker.ServiceClient`."],[2035,"TinkerBackend — thin wrapper around the tinker SDK."],[2543,"TinkerBackend returns tinker's native `SamplingResponse` with\n`.sequences` (one per sample) and optional `.topk_prompt_logprobs`.\nMockBackend returns canned strings for tests."],[2030,"TinkerBackendConfig"],[3001,"TinkerInference"],[3010,"TinkerInference — generate via tinker SamplingClient."],[3007,"TinkerInferenceConfig"],[2950,"TinkerSamplingClient"],[178,"To enable autoresearch we need **standardisation** of experiments — and\n`evsys-sdk` standardises every experiment while staying flexible enough to run\n**any algorithm on any data**."],[859,"To know if training is working, you score the model against a held-out\n**benchmark** while it trains. A benchmark is a **directory** containing a\n`tasks.jsonl` — each task has an `instruction` (the full prompt) and a\n**verifier** that says whether an answer is correct:"],[1118,"To make your store importable from any project without copying code, expose it\nas a Python entry point under the group `evsys_sdk.data_stores` in your\npackage's `pyproject.toml`:"],[1241,"To register a transform from a separate pip package (no SDK edit, no import in\nyour project), declare a Python **entry point** under the group\n`evsys_sdk.transforms` in that package's `pyproject.toml`:"],[2806,"Token-level turns come from `rollout_details` (tinker on-policy rollouts).\nClosed/API models (litellm) return no token ids, so for an eval trial — one\nthat produced a verifier reward — we still build a *token-less* Trajectory\ncarrying the reward + usage so it isn't dropped from scoring. Errored trials,\nand generation-only trials with neither tokens nor a reward, return `None`."],[2936,"Tokenize every :class:`ChatMessagesRow` → list of `tinker.Datum`."],[2306,"Tokenizer-agnostic: any base client exposing a HF-style `_tokenizer`\nattribute works (e.g. `TinkerInference`)."],[714,"top level: `name`, `output_dir`, stores, one of `run`/`runs`/`matrix`, `n_repeats`/`base_seed`, `parent_experiment_id`, `metadata`"],[1363,"Top-level aggregates: `mean_reward`, `pass_rate`, `n_tasks`."],[1695,"Top-level experiment."],[2008,"Top-level structure validated by ExperimentConfig (Pydantic, strict)."],[799,"Train rows carry `reward/mean` (`split: \"train\"`); in-loop val rows carry\n`val/val/pass@1` (`split: \"val\"`). As the policy learns, you watch `reward/mean`\nrise."],[1609,"Train the base `run` once per dataset in `continual.datasets`, in\norder, chaining each stage's final weights (fresh optimizer) into the\nnext. Each completed stage is scored on every benchmark via\n:meth:`_execute_arm`; a chain stops at the first stage that does not\ncomplete."],[218,"Train your first model in five minutes — no GPU, no network — then point it at a real backend."],[203,"Train your first model in five minutes — no GPU, no network."],[1981,"training"],[1660,"Training algorithm (recipe) — one of the registered @register\\_algorithm."],[847,"Training data is a **JSONL file**: one JSON object per line. You bring whatever\nshape your data is in — here, each line is a query and the tool that answers it:"],[1409,"Training step / batch index, if recorded (`batch` in tinker)."],[1563,"Training-side metrics from `RunResult.metrics`."],[1410,"Training-state checkpoint URI (`state_path` in tinker)."],[2833,"TrainingBatch"],[2841,"TrainingLoop"],[2855,"TrainingLoop — algorithm-agnostic driver around a tinker\ntraining client."],[2995,"trajectory"],[2980,"Trajectory"],[2985,"TrajectoryGroup"],[747,"transform"],[100,"Transform"],[1848,"Transform"],[1954,"transforms"],[1222,"Transforms"],[1723,"TransformSpec"],[2110,"Trivial baseline: exact-match (1.0) or substring-match (0.5)."],[1000,"TRL `GRPOTrainer` on the `local` backend, reward driven by a registered verifier (`verifier_kind` / `verifier_params`)."],[998,"TRL `SFTTrainer` on the `local` backend (transformers + peft + trl). LoRA on any HF model, runs on CPU/MPS/CUDA."],[2230,"True if any accepted slug appears in `returned` (a list of slugs)."],[1541,"True iff any message in the row carries at least one image block."],[2989,"Turn"],[2714,"Turn :class:`~evsys_sdk.training.env.TrajectoryGroup`\\s into\n`list[tinker.Datum]` ready for IS-loss training."],[1237,"Turns each raw row into `{..., \"messages\": [...]}`. Adds a `system` message if `system_prompt` is set, a `user` message from `user_template.format(**row)`, and — if `assistant_template` is given (SFT) — an `assistant` message from `assistant_template.format(**row)`. Templates are Python format strings whose `{field}` placeholders pull from the row's keys."],[2728,"Turns with no completion tokens are dropped silently — IS loss is a no-op."],[861,"Two **independent** knobs to understand:"],[1341,"Two builders:"],[1961,"Two layers:"],[2104,"Two modes:"],[1247,"Two reward mechanisms — the Verifier class registry and the in-process verifier-fn registry referenced from task data."],[1517,"Two row formats:"],[1891,"Two row shapes are accepted:"],[1047,"Two safety properties matter: **a raising callback never kills the run** (the\nexception is logged at WARNING and the next callback runs), and **every hook has\na no-op default** so you override only the ones you care about."],[333,"Type"],[379,"Type"],[406,"Type"],[433,"Type"],[445,"Type"],[454,"Type"],[2875,"Unlike training, eval rollouts are **uploaded to the dashboard** (Supabase)\nwith `kind='eval'` via :func:`upload_eval_rollouts`. (Training rollouts stay\non disk in the run workspace and are never uploaded.)"],[1897,"Until now researcher scripts have hand-rolled a forwarder loop after each\ntraining run (see `composio-bench/training/backfill_step_metrics.py`).\nThis module gives them one call:"],[1412,"Untouched manifest row, for fields not modeled above."],[1402,"Upload (or re-upload) a harbor benchmark directory."],[1309,"Upload (or re-upload) a harbor directory via the supplied store callables."],[2882,"Upload eval predictions to the dashboard. Accepts either a\n`DashboardClient` (`log_predictions`) or an `EvsysStore`\n(`add_prediction` per row). No-op when `store`/`run_id` is falsy."],[1391,"UploadResult"],[1621,"Usage:"],[1760,"Usage::"],[294,"Use"],[2978,"Use `add_generation_prompt=True` for sampling prompts (the assistant\nturn isn't included yet; the model writes it). `False` when building\na completed sequence (e.g. SFT teacher-forcing)."],[937,"Use a built-in"],[968,"Use a built-in"],[1013,"Use a built-in"],[1042,"Use a built-in"],[1097,"Use a built-in"],[1126,"Use a built-in"],[1165,"Use a built-in"],[1195,"Use a built-in"],[1225,"Use a built-in"],[1250,"Use a built-in"],[1253,"Use a built-in fn"],[1459,"Use as a context manager. On clean exit, the generation + experiment are\nmarked completed (with the best score / generation\\_id). On raised\nexception, both are marked failed with the exception message. All writes\nare mirrored locally and degrade gracefully if the backend is down."],[2080,"Use case: `SFT warmup → GRPO refine`, `cold-start distill → DAPO`, etc.\nEach phase runs against the same RunContext but writes its artifacts to a\n`phase\\{i\\}_\\{name\\}` subdirectory; the previous phase's `final_checkpoint`\nartifact is threaded into the next phase via `ctx.extras`."],[1785,"Use via the CLI: `evsys init-project \\<name>`. Programmatically: call\n`init_project(path, name=...)`."],[1777,"Use via the CLI: `evsys new-experiment \\<slug>`. Programmatically:\n`new_experiment(project_root, slug)`."],[2629,"Used by EarlyStoppingCallback and similar policies. The loop honours\nit at the top of the next iteration so the current step's writes\nflush cleanly first."],[1922,"Used by evolutionary algorithms to know the legal field space."],[2398,"Useful for `log_store.kind: multiplex` configs:"],[1600,"User-supplied factory wins; otherwise pick a default by backend kind."],[2048,"Validate `ctx.extras` before the backend is allocated. Override to\nfail fast on missing / empty inputs (e.g. no train\\_rows). Default\nno-op."],[2007,"Validation has two layers:"],[595,"Var"],[1853,"VerificationResult"],[759,"verifier"],[88,"Verifier"],[1856,"Verifier"],[263,"Verifier specs (data, not executors)"],[1520,"Verifier specs (the data the runner serializes for HarborTask):"],[761,"verifier specs / RL reward"],[1959,"verifiers"],[1246,"Verifiers"],[1725,"VerifierSpec"],[210,"Verify"],[704,"Vocabulary"],[1941,"Walk a dotted path into a nested-dict tree and set the leaf value."],[60,"Walkthroughs for the most common things you'll do with `evsys-sdk`."],[2809,"Wall-clock seconds for a harbor timing phase — anything carrying\n`started_at` / `finished_at` datetimes. `None` when either is missing."],[2643,"WandbLoggerCallback"],[2648,"WandbLoggerConfig"],[2595,"Watch a metric emitted on eval; request\\_stop after N evals without\nimprovement."],[1072,"Watches a metric on `on_eval` and calls `state.request_stop()` after N evals without improvement. Params: `metric`, `eval_name` (or `None` = any), `patience` (default 3), `mode` (`max`/`min`), `min_delta`."],[176,"We believe there will not be a few generally intelligent models that everyone\nuses, but **thousands of models adapted for every task**, continually learning\nfrom every interaction. To enable this we need infrastructure that lets\n**coding agents launch experiments, learn from them, and train models that\nlearn continuously**. `evsys-sdk` is the first step toward that."],[2972,"We deliberately do NOT reproduce tinker\\_cookbook's `Renderer` class hierarchy\n— Hugging Face's tokenizers already implement the template via\n`apply_chat_template`, and the cookbook's `Renderer` subclasses just wrap\nthat call with per-model defaults (`enable_thinking=False` for Qwen3.5-disable\nvariants, etc.). We forward the kwarg directly when set, which keeps every\nHF chat-template-aware tokenizer working uniformly."],[2911,"We use :func:`~evsys_sdk.training.templates.messages_to_model_input`\nrather than the cookbook's `Renderer.build_generation_prompt` —\nsame end shape (HF chat-template applied with add\\_generation\\_prompt=True),\nno Renderer class hierarchy needed."],[1861,"We use `typing.Protocol` (PEP 544) instead of ABCs so extensions don't have\nto subclass anything from the library — any class that implements the methods\nsatisfies the protocol. This is what makes third-party algorithms / verifiers\n/ metrics trivial to add."],[1616,"What `Experiment.run` returns."],[2522,"What `forward_backward_*_async` resolves to."],[1043,"What `local_logger` writes, exactly"],[1843,"What an algorithm returns from .train(ctx)."],[2366,"What every generate() returns. \\{prompt} placeholder is filled in."],[659,"What it does"],[954,"What it does"],[990,"What it does"],[1027,"What it does"],[1203,"What it does"],[1235,"What it does"],[1266,"What it does"],[1066,"What it does / where it writes"],[1111,"What it does / where it writes"],[1140,"What it does / where it writes"],[1177,"What it does / where it writes"],[1620,"What it replaces in researcher scripts: the manual\n`create_experiment` → `create_group` → per-arm `create_run` →\n`run_experiment(cfg)` → `create_eval` → `set_conclusion` choreography.\nToday every sweep script hand-rolls that loop. An `Experiment` collapses it\nto one declarative `.run()` call."],[2864,"What the loop does NOT own: data shaping. A :class:`StepBuilder` decides\nwhat each batch contains and computes algorithm-specific metrics. That's\nthe seam SFT / SDFT / RL plug into."],[174,"What you can plug in"],[792,"What's in it"],[826,"What's in it"],[867,"What's in it"],[122,"What's NOT in v0.1"],[952,"When `agent_import_path` is `null`, the engine uses\n`BasicLoopAgent`, parameterized by the rollout kwargs above. When you set it to a\n`\"module.path:ClassName\"` string, **that agent wins and the engine passes it no\nkwargs** — it must be fully self-configured."],[69,"When `evsys_sdk` imports, every entry point in that group is\nloaded. No fork needed."],[2240,"When >1 and the client exposes `generate_batch`, submit prompts in\nchunks of this size and collect them concurrently. Falls back to\nsequential `generate` calls if the client doesn't support batching."],[2304,"When a model is SFT'd on chat-templated sequences (HF\n`tokenizer.apply_chat_template` over a system + user + assistant message\nlist), the assistant-side output format only emerges reliably when the\nprompt at inference time is shaped the same way. `Benchmark.score()` hands\nthe client a raw `task.instruction` string with no role markers; this\nwrapper rebuilds the (system + user) opener around it before forwarding to\nthe underlying client."],[1297,"When evsys\\_sdk imports, we walk those groups and import each\ntarget module — its top-level @register\\_\\* decorators run, populating our\nregistries. No fork required."],[855,"When no built-in fits, write your own and reference it by `kind` — no SDK fork:"],[35,"When the run finishes, the SDK scores the arms against your `success_metric&#x60;,\npicks the &#x2A;*`best_arm`**, and synthesizes a **conclusion** — recorded right next\nto the hypothesis (in `experiment.md` and/or the dashboard). Claude Code reads\nthat conclusion, updates its hypothesis, and launches the next experiment."],[785,"When training runs, the policy **rolls out** on `instruction` (generates an\nanswer), and the verifier returns a reward (here: 1.0 if the completion contains\n`<answer>4</answer>`, else 0.0). That reward is the entire learning signal — no\ngold completion is ever shown to the model."],[1699,"Where local artifacts (checkpoints, logs) are written."],[350,"Where local artifacts/logs are written"],[1163,"Where metrics, hyperparameters, and artifact pointers go as training proceeds."],[1819,"Where metrics, hyperparams, and artifact pointers go."],[1680,"Where the training data comes from + how to transform it."],[2935,"Which assistant turns the loss is computed on. This is an *algorithm*\ndecision (passed in by the composer), NOT a property of the dataset —\n:class:`~evsys_sdk.data_types.ChatMessagesRow` carries only the conversation."],[412,"Which built-in loader"],[1682,"Which built-in source loader to use (ignored when dataset\\_id/name set)."],[1714,"Which model to fine-tune."],[115,"Why a registry per kind"],[114,"Why protocols, not ABCs"],[2976,"Why the gate: Qwen3.5 tokenizers accept `enable_thinking`, but most\nothers do NOT and raise on the unknown kwarg. Forwarding only when set\nkeeps the helper tokenizer-agnostic — same approach already in\n`ChatTemplatedInference` (`inference/chat_templated.py`)."],[1610,"With `n_repeats > 1` the *whole chain* is replicated once per seed\n(`[base_seed, base_seed+1, ...]` or `[run.seed, ...]`). Stage *i*\nacross all repeats shares one dashboard group, so variance is aggregated\nper stage. Within a chain, weights are chained only between that chain's\nown stages."],[1472,"with ExperimentRun(client, experiment\\_name=\"sft\\_run\\_v9\",\nrecipe\\_kind=\"sft\",\nrun\\_config=\\{\"lr\": 1e-5, \"batch\\_size\": 16}) as run:\nfor step in range(1, 1001):\nrun.log\\_step(step, loss=...)\nrun.log\\_eval(metrics=\\{\"pass\\_at\\_1\": 0.83}, benchmark\\_id=\"...\")\nrun.set\\_best\\_score(0.83)"],[480,"Without a template, names become `{base}__{lastkey}{value}__...`."],[2280,"Works on any per-row, per-query result shape: the caller supplies a function\nthat maps one query-result to a bool `found`, so the same scorer serves\nmodel evals and any custom eval harness."],[1973,"workspace"],[1969,"Workspace"],[1974,"Workspace — local cache for remote datasets/benchmarks."],[2953,"Wrap a `tinker.SamplingClient` to satisfy the\n:class:`~evsys_sdk.training.backend.SamplingClient` Protocol shape."],[2912,"Wrap a student rollout (prompt + sampled completion) as a `tinker.Datum`."],[1756,"Wrap formatted records in ANSI color based on level (TTY only)."],[2293,"Wraps a callable; retries on a configurable set of exceptions with exponential\nbackoff. Exhausted failures are pushed onto a RetryReport so the eval harness\ncan surface them in the final report rather than aborting."],[2508,"Wraps a training client + factory for sampling clients."],[2301,"Wraps an InferenceClient to apply a chat template before each `generate` call."],[2233,"Wraps verified\\_aliases.json and an optional secondary-aliases file so a\npredicted slug counts as correct if it equals the expected slug OR any\nof the expected slug's verified aliases."],[2609,"Writes `\\<output_dir>/\\<run_key>/` : `metrics.jsonl` (train + val rows),\n`predictions/\\<name>.jsonl` (per benchmark), and `summary.md` at\nrun end. The \"print what's happening\" requirement is the per-step one-liner\n(cadence `print_every`)."],[2089,"writes into phase\\_dir"],[2862,"writing on